true</div><div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-3); font-style:italic; margin-bottom:10px;">actual output, captured from the JVM</div><ol><li>An int holds 32 bits, so its range is fixed.</li><li>Exceeding it wraps around to the most negative value.</li><li>No error, no warning — the program simply continues with a wrong number.</li></ol></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — The fix is a wider type, chosen early</div><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; padding:11px 13px; overflow-x:auto; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0;">int a = 2_000_000_000;
System.out.println(a + a);
long b = 2_000_000_000L;
System.out.println(b + b);
System.out.println((long) a + a);</pre><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--accent); background:var(--surface-2); padding:8px 12px; margin:8px 0 4px; font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap;">-294967296
