nt-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">j=3</text><line x1="126" y1="51" x2="356" y2="51" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#fk74a)"/><text x="408" y="55" fill="#6366f1" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">inner loop (j)</text><text x="408" y="69" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">finishes ALL its passes</text><text x="408" y="81" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">before i moves once</text><text x="260" y="196" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-style="italic">Visit order 1→12: outer i fixed while inner j runs 0..3. Total passes = 3 × 4 = 12.</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div>Count nested-loop output by multiplying the pass counts. If the inner bound depends on i (<code>j &lt;= i</code>), add instead: 1+2+3+... — that pattern is on nearly every OA.</div><i data-tbd286bz47="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — when the inner bound depends on the outer variable, the count is a sum not a product</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 326" style="width:100%; max-width:680px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk229a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="170" y="24" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">rectangular:  c <= 3</text><text x="500" y="24" fill=