font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">10</text><text x="500" y="248" fill="#e8795a" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10 inner passes</text><line x1="300" y1="40" x2="300" y2="232" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/><rect x="20" y="268" width="640" height="46" rx="10" fill="#8b5cf6" opacity="0.10" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="340" y="297" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Multiply only when the inner bound is a constant. If it depends on r, add: n(n+1)/2.</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — a rectangular grid: multiplying the two counts</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">A warehouse has three shelves of four slots. Printing the slot codes is the standard nested pair, and the placement of the second <code>println</code> is the whole exercise.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int cells = 0;
for (int shelf = 1; shelf &lt;= 3; shelf++) {
    for (int slot = 1; slot &lt;= 4; slot++) {
        System.out.print(shelf * slot + " ");
        cells++;
    }
    System.out.println();          // OUTER loop — once per shelf
}
System.out.println("cells " + cells);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>1 2 3 4 
2 4 6 8 
3 6 9 12 
cells 12</div><ol style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px; padding:0; line-height:1.75;"><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">The inner loop runs to completion — all four slots — for every single pass of the outer loop.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">Total inner passes are 3 × 4 = 12, which is what <code>cells</code> confirms.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">The bare <code>println()</code> sits between the inner loop's closing brace and the outer loop's, so it runs three times: once per shelf. Move it one line up, inside the inner braces, and all twelve numbers land on separate lines.</li></ol><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: three rows of four, 12 inner passes</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — a triangular pattern: the inner bound depends on the outer</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The same shape with one change — the inner loop stops at the current row number — and the count stops being a product.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int stars = 0;
for (int r = 1; r &lt;= 4; r++) {
    for (int c = 1; c &lt;= r; c++) {   // bound depends on r
        System.out.print("*");
        stars++;
    }
    System.out.println();
}
System.out.println(stars);</pre><div style="overflow-x:auto; margin:14px 0;"><table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:14.5px;"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">r</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">inner bound c &lt;= r</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">stars this row</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">running total</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">1</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">c = 1</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">1</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">1</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">2</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">c = 1, 2</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">2</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">3</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">3</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">c = 1, 2, 3</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">3</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">6</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">c = 1, 2, 3, 4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>*
