256" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="276" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">i</text><text x="276" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">4</text><rect x="306" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="326" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">t</text><text x="326" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">5</text><rect x="356" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="376" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">e</text><text x="376" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">6</text><rect x="406" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="426" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">.</text><text x="426" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">7</text><rect x="456" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="476" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">n</text><text x="476" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">8</text><rect x="506" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="526" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">e</text><text x="526" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">9</text><rect x="556" y="46" width="40" height="40" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="576" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">t</text><text x="576" y="102" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">10</text><text x="22" y="128" fill="#10b981" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">STICKY:  if (illegal) valid = false;   — can only fall</text><rect x="56" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="76" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="106" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="126" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="156" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="176" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="206" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="226" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="256" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="276" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="306" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="326" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="356" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="376" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="406" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="426" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="456" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="476" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="506" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="526" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="556" y="140" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="576" y="160" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><text x="608" y="160" fill="#10b981" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">false ✓</text><text x="22" y="202" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">RESET:  valid = isLegal(c);   — overwritten every pass</text><rect x="56" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="76" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="106" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="126" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="156" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="176" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">F</text><rect x="206" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="226" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="256" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="276" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="306" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="326" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="356" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="376" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="406" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="426" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="456" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="476" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="506" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="526" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><rect x="556" y="214" width="40" height="30" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="576" y="234" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">T</text><text x="608" y="234" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">true ✗</text><rect x="20" y="268" width="640" height="76" rx="10" fill="#f59e0b" opacity="0.10" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="340" y="300" fill="#f59e0b" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">The reset version reports only the LAST character it looked at.</text><text x="340" y="326" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">A validation flag starts true, may fall to false, and must never climb back.</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — validating a domain with the flag in the loop condition</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Two rules are being checked at once, and they behave differently: "every character is legal" can fail early, while "there is at least one dot" cannot be decided until the end.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">String domain = "shop-01.example.com";
boolean valid = domain.length() &gt;= 3;
boolean hasDot = false;
int i = 0;
while (valid &amp;&amp; i &lt; domain.length()) {          // early exit without break
    char c = domain.charAt(i);
    if (c == '.') hasDot = true;
    else if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(c) &amp;&amp; c != '-') valid = false;
    i++;
}
valid = valid &amp;&amp; hasDot;
System.out.println("chars examined: " + i + ", valid: " + valid);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>chars examined: 19, valid: true</div><ol style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px; padding:0; line-height:1.75;"><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">Every character of "shop-01.example.com" is a letter, a digit, a hyphen or a dot, so <code>valid</code> is never falsified and all 19 characters are examined.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">The two dots set <code>hasDot</code>, and the <code>else if</code> means a dot is never also tested as an illegal character.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;"><code>valid && i &lt; length()</code> puts the early exit in the condition: had character 3 been a space, <code>valid</code> would drop to false and the very next test would end the loop with <code>i</code> at 4 — the same effect as <code>break</code>, with the exit rule visible at the top.</li></ol><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: 19 characters examined, valid: true</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — the assignment that turns a flag into a last-character report</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">One character of difference — <code>valid = ...</code> instead of <code>if (...) valid = false;</code> — and the same input gives the opposite answer.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">String domain = "my site.net";              // illegal space at index 2

boolean valid = true;                       // RESET every pass — wrong
for (int i = 0; i &lt; domain.length(); i++) {
    char c = domain.charAt(i);
    valid = Character.isLetterOrDigit(c) || c == '.' || c == '-';
}
System.out.println("reset-each-pass version says: " + valid);

boolean valid2 = true;                      // STICKY — right
for (int i = 0; i &lt; domain.length(); i++) {
    char c = domain.charAt(i);
    if (!(Character.isLetterOrDigit(c) || c == '.' || c == '-')) valid2 = false;
}
System.out.println("sticky-flag version says: " + valid2);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>reset-each-pass version says: true
sticky-flag version says: false</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The reset version does detect the space at index 2 — and then overwrites that discovery on every later character. By the end it is reporting only whether the final "t" is legal, which it is. The sticky version can only ever move from true to false, so one bad character survives to the answer. Both compile, both run, and only one of them is a validator.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: true from the broken version, false from the correct one</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;"><div class="callout-label">⚠️ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The same fault appears in a "found" flag written the other way round: <code>found = (a[i] == target);</code> inside a loop reports only whether the <em>last</em> element matched. A search flag starts false and may only rise; a validation flag starts true and may only fall. If an assignment inside a loop can move a flag in both directions, it is wrong.</p></div>"},"D286/u5/z5_1":{"body":"<p>Up to now every value needed its own variable. That works for three test scores and collapses at thirty. An <strong>array</strong> is one name holding many values of the same type, reached by position — which is what finally makes the loops of Unit 4 useful for real data.</p><p>Two properties define an array and cause almost every array bug. Its <strong>length is fixed</strong> at creation and can never change, and its <strong>indexes run from 0 to length - 1</strong>.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">scores[0]  scores[1]  scores[2]  scores[3]  scores[4]
   88        92        79        95        61        &lt;- length 5
                                                     &lt;- last index is 4, not 5</pre><p>Because the index is just an <code>int</code>, it can be a loop variable — and that single fact is the whole reason arrays and <code>for</code> loops are taught together.</p><h3>Why index 0, and what the exception tells you</h3><p>An index is not a position in a list, it is an <em>offset</em> from the start of the block of memory. The first element is zero elements from the start, so it is <code>a[0]</code>. Every consequence follows from that one fact.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto; margin:14px 0;"><table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:14.5px;"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:.03em; text-transform:uppercase; opacity:.75;">Array of length 5</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:.03em; text-transform:uppercase; opacity:.75;">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;">first index</td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;">last index</td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>4</code>, written <code>a.length - 1</code></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>a.length</code></td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>5</code> — a count, never a valid index</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>a[5]</code></td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><strong>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException</strong> at run time</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>That exception is a <em>runtime</em> error, not a compile error: the compiler cannot know what the index will be, so nothing warns you. The message names the offending index — "Index 5 out of bounds for length 5" — which tells you immediately that a bound used <code>&lt;=</code> where it needed <code>&lt;</code>.</p><p>The length being fixed at creation is the other half. An array cannot grow; to "add" an element you allocate a bigger array and copy across, which is exactly what <code>ArrayList</code> does for you behind the scenes.</p><i data-d286u5="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Array:</strong> a fixed-size, ordered collection of values of one type, accessed by index</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Index:</strong> the position of an element, starting at 0</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Element:</strong> one value stored in the array</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Length:</strong> the number of elements; fixed when the array is created</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#22c55e;"><div class="callout-label">💡 WHY IT MATTERS</div><p>Everything from here to Unit 14 is a variation on this idea. <code>ArrayList</code> (7.14) is an array that can grow; a <code>HashMap</code> (14.3) is the same lookup idea keyed by something other than a number.</p></div><i data-tbd286bz51="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — why the first index is 0, and why the last one is length − 1</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 312" style="width:100%; max-width:680px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk236a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="340" y="24" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">an index is not a position in a list — it is an OFFSET from the start</text><rect x="66" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="99" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">12</text><text x="99" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[0]</text><text x="99" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">0 away</text><rect x="140" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="173" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0</text><text x="173" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[1]</text><text x="173" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">1 away</text><rect x="214" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="247" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">31</text><text x="247" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[2]</text><text x="247" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">2 away</text><rect x="288" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="321" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">8</text><text x="321" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[3]</text><text x="321" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">3 away</text><rect x="362" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="395" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">26</text><text x="395" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[4]</text><text x="395" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">4 away</text><rect x="436" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="469" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">4</text><text x="469" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[5]</text><text x="469" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">5 away</text><rect x="510" y="56" width="66" height="46" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="543" y="84" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">19</text><text x="543" y="118" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[6]</text><text x="543" y="136" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">6 away</text><line x1="66" y1="168" x2="66" y2="146" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#fk236a)"/><text x="72" y="186" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">start of the block — 0 elements along</text><line x1="66" y1="46" x2="576" y2="46" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="321" y="38" fill="#10b981" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">rainfall.length = 7   (a COUNT, never an index)</text><rect x="66" y="206" width="268" height="92" rx="10" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.10" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="200" y="234" fill="#10b981" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">valid</text><text x="200" y="258" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">rainfall[0]            → 12</text><text x="200" y="280" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">rainfall[length - 1]   → 19</text><rect x="352" y="206" width="292" height="92" rx="10" fill="#e11d48" opacity="0.10" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="498" y="234" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">runtime exception</text><text x="498" y="258" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">rainfall[7]   Index 7 out of bounds</text><text x="498" y="280" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">rainfall[-1]  Index -1 out of bounds</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — reading an array by its bounds</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">A week of rainfall in millimetres. Three questions about it are answered without a loop at all — just by indexing.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] rainfall = {12, 0, 31, 8, 26, 4, 19};
System.out.println("days: " + rainfall.length);
System.out.println("first: " + rainfall[0] + ", last: " + rainfall[rainfall.length - 1]);
System.out.println("third: " + rainfall[2]);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>days: 7
first: 12, last: 19
third: 31</div><ol style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px; padding:0; line-height:1.75;"><li style="margin-bottom:5px;"><code>length</code> is 7 — the number of elements, and it is a <em>field</em>, so there are no parentheses.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;"><code>rainfall[0]</code> is the first element, 12. Zero elements along from the start.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;"><code>rainfall[rainfall.length - 1]</code> is <code>rainfall[6]</code>, the last one, 19. Learn that whole expression as one symbol meaning "the last".</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">"Third" in ordinary speech is index <strong>2</strong>, not 3. That off-by-one between how people count and how arrays are indexed is the source of most of the confusion in this unit.</li></ol><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Note that <code>rainfall[1]</code> is 0 — a real recorded value of zero millimetres. A stored 0 and an absent element are different things, which matters once the array is longer than the data.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: 7 days; first 12, last 19; the third day is 31</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — what going out of bounds actually reports</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The exception is worth meeting deliberately once, because its message names the mistake precisely.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] rainfall = {12, 0, 31, 8, 26, 4, 19};
try { System.out.println(rainfall[7]); }
catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) { System.out.println("threw: " + e.getMessage()); }
try { System.out.println(rainfall[-1]); }
catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) { System.out.println("threw: " + e.getMessage()); }</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>threw: Index 7 out of bounds for length 7
threw: Index -1 out of bounds for length 7</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Two things to take from this. First, index 7 on a length-7 array is <em>one past the end</em>, and the message says so in exactly those words — so when you see it in a real run, the fix is almost always a loop bound written <code>&lt;=</code> that should be <code>&lt;</code>. Second, this is a <strong>runtime</strong> exception, not a compile error: <code>rainfall[7]</code> compiles happily, because the compiler cannot in general know what an index will be.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: both throw ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException, naming the index and the length</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;"><div class="callout-label">⚠️ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;"><code>length</code> is a count and indexes are offsets, so they never match. An array of length 7 has no element 7. The moment you write <code>a[a.length]</code> — or a loop bound of <code>i &lt;= a.length</code> — you have asked for one element past the end, and the program will get all the way to the final pass before telling you.</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">When a question gives you an array and asks for "the last element" or "the middle element", write the index as an expression in <code>length</code> rather than a number: <code>a[a.length - 1]</code> and <code>a[a.length / 2]</code>. Answers that hard-code a number are the distractors, because they break the moment the length changes.</p></div>"},"D286/u5/z5_2":{"body":"<p>There are three ways to bring an array into existence, and choosing between them comes down to whether you already know the values.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int[] a = new int[5];              // 5 elements, all 0 by default
int[] b = {10, 20, 30};            // literal — length 3, inferred
int[] c;  c = new int[]{1, 2, 3};  // the long form of the literal

a[0] = 88;                         // store
int x = a[0];                      // read
int n = a.length;                  // LENGTH — a field, no parentheses</pre><p>New arrays are filled with the default for their type, and the defaults come from the same table as fields in 2.2: <code>0</code> for numeric types, <code>false</code> for boolean, <code>null</code> for objects and Strings. That last one matters — a new <code>String[]</code> is an array of nulls, not of empty strings.</p><h3>Three ways to create one, and what is in it</h3><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int[] a = new int[5];                 // 5 elements, all 0
int[] b = {10, 20, 30};               // literal — size taken from the list
int[] c;                              // declared, refers to nothing yet
c = new int[3];                       // now it exists

int[] d = {1,2,3};                    // only legal AT the declaration
d = {4,5,6};                          // compile error
d = new int[]{4,5,6};                 // this is the way to reassign</pre><div style="overflow-x:auto; margin:14px 0;"><table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:14.5px;"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:.03em; text-transform:uppercase; opacity:.75;">Element type</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:.03em; text-transform:uppercase; opacity:.75;">Default value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>int</code>, <code>long</code>, <code>short</code>, <code>byte</code></td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>double</code>, <code>float</code></td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>0.0</code></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>char</code></td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>'\u0000'</code> — prints as blank</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>boolean</code></td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><code>String</code> and any object</td><td style="padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); vertical-align:top;"><strong><code>null</code></strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The last row is the one that bites. <code>new String[3]</code> gives three <code>null</code>s, not three empty strings, so calling <code>.length()</code> on any of them throws a <code>NullPointerException</code> until you assign real values.</p><i data-d286u5="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>new int[5]:</strong> creates an array of 5 elements, each set to the type default</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Array literal:</strong> the {…} form that creates and fills an array in one step</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>length:</strong> a public final field on every array; note that String uses length() instead</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Default value:</strong> 0, 0.0, false or null depending on the element type</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="warn" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;"><div class="callout-label">⚠ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p><code>arr.length()</code> does not compile — arrays use the field <code>length</code>, Strings use the method <code>length()</code>. Reversing them is one of the most reliably tested details in the course (see 4.6).</p></div><p data-xref="1" style="margin:26px 0 0; padding-top:12px; border-top:1px solid var(--border);font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.72;">✅ Also covered in depth: <strong>Arrays → 1D Arrays</strong></p><i data-d286fx8="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — AN ARRAY IS NUMBERED BOXES, STARTING AT 0</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 500 142" style="width:100%; max-width:540px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk75a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="30" y="26" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">int[] scores = {72, 85, 91, 60, 78};</text><rect x="60" y="44" width="62" height="44" rx="0" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="91" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">72</text><text x="91" y="106" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[0]</text><rect x="122" y="44" width="62" height="44" rx="0" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="153" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">85</text><text x="153" y="106" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[1]</text><rect x="184" y="44" width="62" height="44" rx="0" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="215" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">91</text><text x="215" y="106" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[2]</text><rect x="246" y="44" width="62" height="44" rx="0" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="277" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">60</text><text x="277" y="106" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[3]</text><rect x="308" y="44" width="62" height="44" rx="0" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="339" y="71" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">78</text><text x="339" y="106" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[4]</text><rect x="370" y="44" width="62" height="44" rx="0" fill="none" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><text x="401" y="71" fill="#ef4444" font-size="15" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">✖</text><text x="401" y="106" fill="#ef4444" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[5]</text><text x="245" y="132" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">scores.length = 5 — valid indexes 0..4. scores[5] throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException.</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div>The last valid index is always <code>length - 1</code>. Loops written <code>i &lt;= scores.length</code> crash on the final pass — spot that <code>&lt;=</code> instantly.</div><i data-tbd286bz52="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — what is actually in an array the instant it is created</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 374" style="width:100%; max-width:680px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk237a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="340" y="24" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">a new array is not empty — it is full of the type default</text><text x="20" y="78" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">int[] counts = new int[4];</text><rect x="268" y="58" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="297" y="81" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0</text><rect x="334" y="58" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="363" y="81" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0</text><rect x="400" y="58" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="429" y="81" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0</text><rect x="466" y="58" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="495" y="81" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0</text><text x="540" y="82" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">0 for the integer types</text><text x="20" y="140" fill="#10b981" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">double[] avgs = new double[4];</text><rect x="268" y="120" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="297" y="143" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0.0</text><rect x="334" y="120" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="363" y="143" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0.0</text><rect x="400" y="120" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="429" y="143" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0.0</text><rect x="466" y="120" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="495" y="143" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0.0</text><text x="540" y="144" fill="#10b981" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">0.0 for double and float</text><text x="20" y="202" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">boolean[] seen = new boolean[4];</text><rect x="268" y="182" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="297" y="205" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">false</text><rect x="334" y="182" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="363" y="205" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">false</text><rect x="400" y="182" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="429" y="205" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">false</text><rect x="466" y="182" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="495" y="205" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">false</text><text x="540" y="206" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">false for boolean</text><text x="20" y="264" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">String[] names = new String[4];</text><rect x="268" y="244" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="297" y="267" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">null</text><rect x="334" y="244" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="363" y="267" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">null</text><rect x="400" y="244" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="429" y="267" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">null</text><rect x="466" y="244" width="58" height="36" rx="7" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="495" y="267" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">null</text><text x="540" y="268" fill="#e11d48" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">null for every object type</text><rect x="20" y="306" width="640" height="56" rx="10" fill="#e11d48" opacity="0.10" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="340" y="332" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">new String[4] gives four nulls, NOT four empty strings —</text><text x="340" y="352" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">names[0].length() throws NullPointerException until something is assigned</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — three ways to create an array, and what is in each</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Creation with <code>new</code> fills every slot with the type default; creation from a literal fills it with your values and infers the length.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] counts     = new int[4];
double[] avgs    = new double[2];
boolean[] flags  = new boolean[2];
String[] names   = new String[3];
System.out.println(counts[0] + " " + avgs[0] + " " + flags[0] + " " + names[0]);
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(counts) + " " + Arrays.toString(names));
int[] b = {10, 20, 30};
System.out.println("literal length " + b.length);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>0 0.0 false null
[0, 0, 0, 0] [null, null, null]
literal length 3</div><ol style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px; padding:0; line-height:1.75;"><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">The defaults are the same table as uninitialised <em>fields</em>: 0 for the integer types, 0.0 for the floating types, false for boolean, null for anything that is an object.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;"><code>Arrays.toString</code> is the readable way to print a whole array; printing the array variable itself gives something like <code>[I@1b6d3586</code>, which is the type and a hash, not the contents.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">The literal form <code>{10, 20, 30}</code> takes its length from the list — three elements, so <code>length</code> is 3, and no size is written anywhere.</li></ol><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The literal form is only legal <em>at the declaration</em>. <code>b = {40, 50, 60};</code> on a later line does not compile; the reassignment form is <code>b = new int[]{40, 50, 60};</code>.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: 0, 0.0, false, null — and a literal length of 3</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — the null that an array of objects hands you</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">An array of Strings is an array of <em>references</em>, and a new one holds no Strings at all.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">String[] codes = new String[3];
codes[0] = "AB1";
System.out.println(codes[0].length());
try { System.out.println(codes[1].length()); }
catch (NullPointerException e) { System.out.println("NullPointerException on codes[1]"); }</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>3
NullPointerException on codes[1]</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;"><code>codes[0]</code> was assigned, so it refers to a real String and <code>length()</code> works. <code>codes[1]</code> is still <code>null</code> — it refers to nothing — so calling any method on it fails at run time. Note what did <em>not</em> happen: <code>codes[1]</code> is a perfectly valid index, so this is not an out-of-bounds problem. The array exists and has three slots; two of them are simply empty.</p><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">This is why a loop over an array of objects often needs <code>if (codes[i] != null)</code> where a loop over an array of ints needs nothing — an <code>int</code> cannot be null, so it always has a usable value.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: 3, then a NullPointerException on the unassigned element</div></div>"},"D286/u5/z5_3":{"body":"<p>Before writing array code, it is worth being fluent at reading it, because most exam array questions are traces rather than constructions. The drill is always the same: draw the array, draw the index, update both line by line.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int[] a = {4, 8, 15, 16, 23};

a[2]            // 15
a[a.length - 1] // 23  — the idiom for "last element"
a[0] + a[4]     // 27
a[a[0]]         // a[4] -&gt; 23   — an element used as an index

for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) { a[i] = a[i] * 2; }
// {8, 16, 30, 32, 46}</pre><p><code>a[a.length - 1]</code> is worth learning as a single symbol for "the last one". Writing <code>a[a.length]</code> instead is the most common runtime crash in Java, and the exception names the index it tried.</p><h3>How to trace an array question</h3><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int[] a = {4, 8, 15, 16};
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) sum += a[i];

  i    a[i]    sum
  0      4       4
  1      8      12
  2     15      27
  3     16      43
  4    stop — 4 &lt; 4 is false</pre><p>Write the table. Every trace question in this unit is answerable in under a minute this way, and reasoning about it in your head is where the mistakes come from. Track exactly the variables the question asks about, one row per pass.</p><p>The two boundary rows are the ones worth checking twice: the first pass, where an accumulator's starting value shows up, and the row where the condition fails, which decides whether the last element was included.</p><i data-d286u5="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException:</strong> the runtime exception thrown when an index is negative or ≥ length</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Bounds:</strong> the valid index range, 0 through length - 1</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Trace table:</strong> a hand-drawn table of index and element values used to follow array code</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="oa" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div><p>The exception is a <em>runtime</em> error, not a compile error (1.4). <code>a[10]</code> on a 5-element array compiles fine — Java only checks the index while running.</p></div><i data-tbd286bz53="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — the trace table: one column per variable, one row per test</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 366" style="width:100%; max-width:680px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk238a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="340" y="24" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">int[] a = {4, 8, 15, 16, 23};   int sum = 0;   for (i = 0; i < a.length; i++) sum += a[i];</text><rect x="190" y="46" width="58" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="219" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">4</text><text x="219" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[0]</text><rect x="256" y="46" width="58" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="285" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">8</text><text x="285" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[1]</text><rect x="322" y="46" width="58" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="351" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">15</text><text x="351" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[2]</text><rect x="388" y="46" width="58" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="417" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">16</text><text x="417" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[3]</text><rect x="454" y="46" width="58" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="483" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">23</text><text x="483" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[4]</text><line x1="351" y1="132" x2="351" y2="114" stroke="#e8795a" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#fk238a)"/><rect x="289.2" y="137" width="123.6" height="22" rx="11" fill="#e8795a" opacity="0.16"/><text x="351" y="152" fill="#e8795a" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">i = 2 reads a[2]</text><text x="185" y="182" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">i</text><text x="260" y="182" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">a[i]</text><text x="390" y="182" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">sum after</text><line x1="150" y1="188" x2="480" y2="188" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="185" y="206" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">0</text><text x="260" y="206" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">4</text><text x="390" y="206" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">4</text><line x1="150" y1="212" x2="480" y2="212" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="185" y="230" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">1</text><text x="260" y="230" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">8</text><text x="390" y="230" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">12</text><line x1="150" y1="236" x2="480" y2="236" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="185" y="254" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">2</text><text x="260" y="254" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">15</text><text x="390" y="254" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">27</text><line x1="150" y1="260" x2="480" y2="260" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="185" y="278" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">3</text><text x="260" y="278" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">16</text><text x="390" y="278" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">43</text><line x1="150" y1="284" x2="480" y2="284" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="185" y="302" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">4</text><text x="260" y="302" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">23</text><text x="390" y="302" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">66</text><line x1="150" y1="308" x2="480" y2="308" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="185" y="326" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">5</text><text x="260" y="326" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">—</text><text x="390" y="326" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">test 5 < 5 fails</text><line x1="150" y1="332" x2="480" y2="332" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="340" y="348" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">One row per TEST. The last row is the one that ends the loop — and it has no a[i].</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — tracing a sum, and an element used as an index</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The drill is always the same: write the array once, then a column for each variable the question mentions.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] a = {4, 8, 15, 16, 23};
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) sum += a[i];
System.out.println("sum " + sum);
System.out.println("a[a[0]] is " + a[a[0]]);
System.out.println("last " + a[a.length - 1]);</pre><div style="overflow-x:auto; margin:14px 0;"><table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:14.5px;"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">i</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">i &lt; 5</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">a[i]</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">sum after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">0</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">true</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">4</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">1</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">true</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">8</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">12</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">2</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">true</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">15</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">27</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">3</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">true</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">16</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">43</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">true</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">23</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">66</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">5</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);"><strong>false</strong></td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">—</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">66 — loop ends</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>sum 66
a[a[0]] is 23
last 23</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;"><code>a[a[0]]</code> is read from the inside out: <code>a[0]</code> is 4, so the expression is <code>a[4]</code>, which is 23. An element used as an index is legal because an index is just an <code>int</code> — and it is a favourite exam construction precisely because it forces you to evaluate in the right order.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: sum 66; a[a[0]] is 23; last is 23</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — modifying every element in place</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Reading an element and writing one look almost identical, and the difference is which side of the assignment the subscript is on.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] a = {4, 8, 15, 16, 23};
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) {
    a[i] = a[i] * 2;        // read a[i], double it, write it back
}
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(a));</pre><div style="overflow-x:auto; margin:14px 0;"><table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:14.5px;"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">i</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">a[i] before</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">a[i] after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">0</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">8</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">1</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">8</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">16</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">2</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">15</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">30</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">3</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">16</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">32</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">4</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">23</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">46</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>[8, 16, 30, 32, 46]</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The array itself changed — there is no second array anywhere. That is what "in place" means, and it is only possible with the indexed loop: the enhanced for loop of 5.10 hands you a copy of each element and cannot write back.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: [8, 16, 30, 32, 46]</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;"><div class="callout-label">⚠️ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">When a trace question changes the array <em>while</em> traversing it, your table needs a column for the array too, not just for the loop variable. A line like <code>a[i] = a[i + 1];</code> reads a value that a later pass will overwrite, so tracing with the original values gives a confident wrong answer. Redraw the array row after every pass that writes to it.</p></div>"},"D286/u5/z5_4":{"body":"<p>Four loop patterns cover the overwhelming majority of array work, and recognising which one a question wants is most of the answer.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">// 1. SUM / AVERAGE
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) { sum += a[i]; }
double avg = (double) sum / a.length;      // cast, or integer division (2.5)

// 2. MAXIMUM  — start from the first element, never from 0
int max = a[0];
for (int i = 1; i &lt; a.length; i++) { if (a[i] &gt; max) { max = a[i]; } }

// 3. SEARCH   — index declared OUTSIDE so it survives the loop (4.10)
int found = -1;
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) { if (a[i] == target) { found = i; break; } }

// 4. COUNT matching a condition
int evens = 0;
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) { if (a[i] % 2 == 0) { evens++; } }</pre><p>The maximum pattern is where people lose marks. Initialising <code>max = 0</code> works only if the data is guaranteed non-negative; with all-negative data it returns 0, a value not even in the array. Starting from <code>a[0]</code> is always right.</p><h3>The four patterns, and the maximum trap</h3><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int sum = 0;                          // TOTAL
for (int x : a) sum += x;

int count = 0;                        // COUNT MATCHING
for (int x : a) if (x &gt; 10) count++;

int max = a[0];                       // MAXIMUM — start from a real element
for (int i = 1; i &lt; a.length; i++) if (a[i] &gt; max) max = a[i];

int found = -1;                       // SEARCH — index, or -1 for absent
for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) if (a[i] == target) { found = i; break; }</pre><p>Starting <code>max = 0</code> is the classic error: on all-negative data it returns 0, which is not even in the array. Starting from <code>a[0]</code> is always correct — and start the loop at <code>i = 1</code>, since element 0 is already accounted for.</p><p>The search pattern returns <strong>−1</strong> rather than 0 for "not found", because 0 is a legitimate index. Callers must test <code>found &gt;= 0</code>, not <code>found</code> being truthy — Java will not let you do the latter anyway.</p><i data-d286u5="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Linear search:</strong> checking each element in turn until a match is found; O(n) — see 17.1</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Sentinel -1:</strong> the conventional "not found" result, matching indexOf in 3.16</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Running maximum:</strong> a variable holding the largest value seen so far</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="warn" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;"><div class="callout-label">⚠ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p><code>sum / a.length</code> with two ints performs integer division and truncates. Cast one side to <code>double</code> first — the same trap as 2.5, now with arrays.</p></div><p data-xref="1" style="margin:26px 0 0; padding-top:12px; border-top:1px solid var(--border);font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.72;">✅ Also covered in depth: <strong>Arrays → 1D Arrays</strong></p><i data-tbd286bz54="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — the running maximum: where the starting value comes from</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 298" style="width:100%; max-width:680px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk239a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="340" y="24" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">int[] temps = {-3, -11, -7, -19, -5};   // overnight lows, all below zero</text><rect x="178" y="46" width="62" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="209" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">-3</text><text x="209" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[0]</text><rect x="248" y="46" width="62" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="279" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">-11</text><text x="279" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[1]</text><rect x="318" y="46" width="62" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="349" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">-7</text><text x="349" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[2]</text><rect x="388" y="46" width="62" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="419" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">-19</text><text x="419" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[3]</text><rect x="458" y="46" width="62" height="42" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="489" y="72" fill="var(--text)" font-size="14" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">-5</text><text x="489" y="104" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">[4]</text><rect x="24" y="116" width="306" height="168" rx="10" fill="#e11d48" opacity="0.10" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="36" y="134" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">int max = 0;   ← the classic bug</text><text x="56" y="156" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[0] = -3  >  0 ?  no</text><text x="56" y="180" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[1] = -11  >  0 ?  no</text><text x="56" y="204" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[2] = -7  >  0 ?  no</text><text x="56" y="228" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[3] = -19  >  0 ?  no</text><text x="56" y="252" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[4] = -5  >  0 ?  no</text><text x="177" y="274" fill="#e11d48" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">answer 0 — not in the array at all</text><rect x="350" y="116" width="306" height="168" rx="10" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.10" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="362" y="134" fill="#10b981" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">int max = temps[0];   ← always right</text><text x="382" y="156" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">max = -3   (start from a real element)</text><text x="382" y="180" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[1] = -11 > -3 ?  no</text><text x="382" y="204" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[2] =  -7 > -3 ?  no</text><text x="382" y="228" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[3] = -19 > -3 ?  no</text><text x="382" y="252" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">temps[4] =  -5 > -3 ?  no</text><text x="503" y="274" fill="#10b981" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">answer −3 — the real maximum</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — the maximum that is not in the array</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Five overnight temperatures, every one below freezing. Two versions of the same loop differ only in the starting value of <code>max</code>.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] temps = {-3, -11, -7, -19, -5};

int wrong = 0;                                  // starts outside the data
for (int i = 0; i &lt; temps.length; i++) if (temps[i] &gt; wrong) wrong = temps[i];

int right = temps[0];                           // starts from a real element
for (int i = 1; i &lt; temps.length; i++) if (temps[i] &gt; right) right = temps[i];

System.out.println("max=0 start: " + wrong + "   max=a[0] start: " + right);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>max=0 start: 0   max=a[0] start: -3</div><ol style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px; padding:0; line-height:1.75;"><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">In the first loop nothing is ever greater than 0, so no assignment happens and the reported maximum is 0 — a value that appears nowhere in the data.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">In the second, <code>max</code> starts at <code>temps[0]</code> = −3, which <em>is</em> in the data, and no later element beats it.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">The second loop starts at <code>i = 1</code>, because element 0 has already been accounted for. Starting at 0 is harmless — it just compares −3 with itself once.</li></ol><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The same reasoning applies to a minimum, with <code>Integer.MAX_VALUE</code> as the only other defensible starting point. Starting from <code>a[0]</code> needs no such constant and works for any data — its one requirement is that the array is not empty, which is worth a guard.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: 0 from the broken version, −3 from the correct one</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — an average that loses its fraction</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Summing is easy; the division is where the marks are lost.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">int[] scores = {88, 92, 79, 95, 60};
int sum = 0;
for (int x : scores) sum += x;
System.out.println("sum " + sum);
System.out.println("int division: " + (sum / scores.length));
System.out.println("cast first:   " + ((double) sum / scores.length));</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>sum 414
int division: 82
cast first:   82.8</div><ol style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px; padding:0; line-height:1.75;"><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">414 and 5 are both <code>int</code>, so <code>sum / scores.length</code> is integer division: 82.8 is truncated to 82, and the 0.8 is gone before anything else happens.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;">Assigning that to a <code>double</code> afterwards does not rescue it — <code>double avg = sum / scores.length;</code> stores 82.0.</li><li style="margin-bottom:5px;"><code>(double) sum</code> makes the left operand a double, so the whole division is done in floating point and gives 82.8. Casting either side works; casting the result does not.</li></ol><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">A second detail hides here: <code>scores.length</code> is the divisor only when the array is a perfect fit for the data. Over an oversize array it must be the element count instead, or the unused zeros drag the average down.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: 82 from integer division, 82.8 done correctly</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Recognise the four patterns by their <em>starting value</em>, which is the fastest way to spot a broken one on sight: a total starts at 0, a product starts at 1, a count starts at 0, a maximum starts at <code>a[0]</code>, and a search result starts at −1. If a snippet's initialiser is not on that list, look hard at it before you trace anything.</p></div>"},"D286/u5/z5_5":{"body":"<p>Parallel arrays hold related data in separate arrays where the same index refers to the same thing: <code>names[3]</code> and <code>scores[3]</code> describe one student. It works, and it is how you handle records before Unit 7 gives you classes.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">String[] names  = {"Ada", "Alan", "Grace"};
int[]    scores = {95, 88, 99};

for (int i = 0; i &lt; names.length; i++) {
    System.out.println(names[i] + ": " + scores[i]);
}

// finding the name of the top scorer means tracking the INDEX, not the value
int best = 0;
for (int i = 1; i &lt; scores.length; i++) { if (scores[i] &gt; scores[best]) { best = i; } }
System.out.println("top: " + names[best]);</pre><p>The fragility is that nothing links the arrays. Sort one and the correspondence is destroyed silently. That weakness is the argument for classes in 7.6 — one <code>Student</code> object keeps its own name and score together, so they cannot drift apart.</p><h3>Keeping parallel arrays in step</h3><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">String[] names  = {"Ana", "Ben", "Cy"};
int[]    scores = {88, 71, 95};
// names[i] and scores[i] describe the SAME student

for (int i = 0; i &lt; names.length; i++)
    System.out.println(names[i] + ": " + scores[i]);</pre><p>Three rules keep them usable. They must be the same length; every insert or delete must touch <em>all</em> of them; and any sort must move all of them together, which means sorting by hand rather than calling <code>Arrays.sort</code> on one of them.</p><p><code>Arrays.sort(scores)</code> is precisely the operation that destroys the data: the scores end up in order and the names do not move, so every student now has somebody else's mark. Nothing throws, nothing warns — the program keeps running with silently wrong data. That is the argument for a <code>Student</code> class in 7.6.</p><i data-d286u5="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Parallel arrays:</strong> two or more arrays where matching indexes describe one entity</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Index of maximum:</strong> tracking the position of the largest value rather than the value itself</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#22c55e;"><div class="callout-label">💡 WHY IT MATTERS</div><p>When you meet "choosing classes to create" in 7.6, this is the problem it is answering. Parallel arrays are the before picture.</p></div><i data-tbd286bz55="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — parallel arrays are held together by the index and by nothing else</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 282" style="width:100%; max-width:680px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk240a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><text x="170" y="24" fill="#10b981" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">in step</text><text x="505" y="24" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">after Arrays.sort(scores)</text><line x1="340" y1="44" x2="340" y2="196" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/><text x="50" y="76" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="end">names</text><text x="50" y="140" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="end">scores</text><rect x="66" y="56" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="108" y="77" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">"Ada"</text><rect x="66" y="120" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="108" y="141" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">88</text><text x="108" y="104" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">index 0</text><line x1="108" y1="88" x2="108" y2="120" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><rect x="158" y="56" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="200" y="77" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">"Grace"</text><rect x="158" y="120" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="200" y="141" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">95</text><text x="200" y="104" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">index 1</text><line x1="200" y1="88" x2="200" y2="120" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><rect x="250" y="56" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="292" y="77" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">"Alan"</text><rect x="250" y="120" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.13)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="292" y="141" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">71</text><text x="292" y="104" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">index 2</text><line x1="292" y1="88" x2="292" y2="120" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><rect x="370" y="56" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="412" y="77" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">"Ada"</text><rect x="370" y="120" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="412" y="141" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">71</text><text x="412" y="104" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">index 0</text><line x1="412" y1="88" x2="412" y2="120" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><rect x="462" y="56" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="504" y="77" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">"Grace"</text><rect x="462" y="120" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="504" y="141" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">88</text><text x="504" y="104" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">index 1</text><line x1="504" y1="88" x2="504" y2="120" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><rect x="554" y="56" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(14,165,233,0.13)" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="596" y="77" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">"Alan"</text><rect x="554" y="120" width="84" height="32" rx="7" fill="rgba(225,29,72,0.13)" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="596" y="141" fill="var(--text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">95</text><text x="596" y="104" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">index 2</text><line x1="596" y1="88" x2="596" y2="120" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><text x="170" y="184" fill="#10b981" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Ada 88, Grace 95, Alan 71 ✓</text><text x="505" y="184" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Ada 71, Grace 88, Alan 95 ✗</text><rect x="24" y="206" width="636" height="62" rx="10" fill="#f59e0b" opacity="0.10" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="342" y="232" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Nothing links the two arrays. Sorting one moves its values and leaves the other alone,</text><text x="342" y="254" fill="#f59e0b" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">so every student silently acquires somebody else's mark. No error is ever raised.</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — finding the name of the top scorer</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">The value alone is not the answer here — the question asks <em>who</em>, so the loop must track the index rather than the maximum score.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">String[] names = {"Ada", "Grace", "Alan"};
int[] scores   = {88, 95, 71};

int best = 0;                                     // an INDEX, not a score
for (int i = 1; i &lt; scores.length; i++)
    if (scores[i] &gt; scores[best]) best = i;
System.out.println("top: " + names[best] + " with " + scores[best]);

int worst = 0;
for (int i = 1; i &lt; scores.length; i++)
    if (scores[i] &lt; scores[worst]) worst = i;
System.out.println("bottom: " + names[worst] + " with " + scores[worst]);</pre><div style="overflow-x:auto; margin:14px 0;"><table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:14.5px;"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">i</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">scores[i]</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">scores[best]</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border); font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.04em;">best after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">—</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">—</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">88 (index 0)</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">0</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">1</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">95</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">88</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);"><strong>1</strong> — 95 beats 88</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-weight:600;">2</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">71</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">95</td><td style="padding:6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">1 — unchanged</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>top: Grace with 95
bottom: Alan with 71</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Because <code>best</code> holds a position, it unlocks <em>both</em> arrays: <code>names[best]</code> and <code>scores[best]</code> describe one student. Had the loop tracked <code>int bestScore = scores[0];</code> instead, it would know the mark was 95 and have no way back to the name.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: Grace with 95; Alan with 71</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — the one line that destroys the data</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Sorting looks like an obvious improvement, and on parallel arrays it is a data-loss bug.</p><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); padding:12px 14px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55; margin:10px 0; border:1px solid var(--border);">String[] names = {"Ada", "Grace", "Alan"};
int[] scores   = {88, 95, 71};
Arrays.sort(scores);                    // moves scores only
for (int i = 0; i &lt; names.length; i++)
    System.out.println(names[i] + ": " + scores[i]);</pre><div style="margin:8px 0 10px; border-left:3px solid #10b981; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; padding:8px 12px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap; line-height:1.6;"><span style="display:block; font-family:inherit; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.08em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:4px;">OUTPUT</span>Ada: 71
Grace: 88
Alan: 95</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Every line is wrong, and nothing threw. <code>Arrays.sort</code> rearranged <code>scores</code> into 71, 88, 95 and never touched <code>names</code>, so index 0 now pairs Ada with Alan's mark. The program is still running, the output still looks like a report, and the data is ruined.</p><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Sorting parallel arrays correctly means writing the sort yourself and swapping <em>both</em> arrays on every exchange — which is precisely the bookkeeping a <code>Student</code> class removes, because then one swap moves the name and the mark together.</p><div style="margin-top:8px; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700;">Answer: Ada: 71, Grace: 88, Alan: 95 — every pairing broken</div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;"><div class="callout-label">⚠️ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">Parallel arrays must be the same length and must be edited together. Inserting into one and forgetting the other shifts everything after that point by one, so the data looks correct at the start of the array and is wrong from the insertion point onward — which is the hardest kind of bug to see in a spot check.</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div><p style="margin:10px 0; line-height:1.7;">When an exam question tracks "the position of the largest" rather than the largest itself, that is the parallel-array pattern and the answer needs <code>names[best]</code>. Watch for the distractor that compares <code>scores[i] &gt; best</code> — comparing a score against an index — which compiles and produces nonsense.</p></div>"},"D286/u5/z5_6":{"body":"<p>Swapping two values needs a third variable, and the reason is worth stating precisely: assignment overwrites, so the first assignment destroys the value you still need.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int temp = a;
a = b;
b = temp;

// the broken version
a = b;      // a's original value is now GONE
b = a;      // b gets b's own value — both end up as b</pre><p>In an array the swap is the same, just with indexes, and it is the primitive operation underneath reversing (5.8), selection sort (17.6) and quicksort (17.8).</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int temp = arr[i];
arr[i] = arr[j];
arr[j] = temp;</pre><h3>Why the third variable is unavoidable</h3><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int x = 3, y = 7;

x = y;          // x is now 7 — the original 3 is GONE
y = x;          // y = 7. Both are 7. The swap failed.

int temp = x;   // save what is about to be overwritten
x = y;
y = temp;       // x = 7, y = 3</pre><p>Assignment overwrites, and nothing keeps a copy. The temporary exists to hold the value that the first assignment is about to destroy — which is why the order <em>save, overwrite, restore</em> is fixed.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">int t = a[i]; a[i] = a[j]; a[j] = t;   // the same thing with indexes</pre><p>The arithmetic trick <code>x = x + y; y = x - y; x = x - y;</code> does swap two numbers without a temp, and it is a bad answer on an exam and worse in code: it overflows for large values, breaks for floating-point precision, and does not work at all for objects or Strings.</p><i data-d286u5="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Swap:</strong> exchanging the values of two variables, requiring one temporary</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Temporary variable:</strong> a variable that briefly holds a value so it is not overwritten</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="oa" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div><p>A method cannot swap two <code>int</code> parameters, because primitives are passed by value (6.8). It can swap two array elements, because the array reference gives it access to the original array (6.10).</p></div><i data-d286fx9="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — SWAP NEEDS A THIRD BOX</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 470 166" style="width:100%; max-width:520px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.or