1000</div><div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-3); font-style:italic; margin-bottom:10px;">actual output, captured from the JVM</div><ol><li>A thousand elements are searched in a handful of comparisons.</li><li>Each step halves the range, so the cost grows as log₂ n.</li><li>A linear search would have taken up to 1,000.</li></ol></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div>Binary search REQUIRES a sorted array. If a question shows an unsorted array, binary search is the wrong answer however tempting the numbers look.</div>"},"D286/u11/z11_4":{"body":"<p>Debugging recursion with print statements is the technique from 4.8, with one addition that makes all the difference: print the depth, so you can see the shape rather than a flat list.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">public static int fact(int n, int depth) {
    String pad = "  ".repeat(depth);
    System.out.println(pad + "enter n=" + n);

    if (n &lt;= 1) {
        System.out.println(pad + "base -&gt; 1");
        return 1;
    }
    int result = n * fact(n - 1, depth + 1);
    System.out.println(pad + "exit  n=" + n + " -&gt; " + result);
    return result;
}</pre><p>Printing on the way in and on the way out is what shows you the two phases: descending to the base case, then combining on the way back up. Most recursion bugs are visible in the exit lines, because that is where the combining happens.</p><pre style="background:var(--bg-2, var(--surface-2)); padding:12px; border-radius:8px; font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.55;">static int fact(int n, int depth) {
    System.out.println("  ".repeat(depth) + "enter n=" + n);
    if (n &lt;= 1) { System.out.println("  ".repeat(depth) + "base -&gt; 1"); return 1; }
    int r = n * fact(n - 1, depth + 1);
    System.out.println("  ".repeat(depth) + "return " + r);
    return r;
}</pre><p>Print on the way <em>in</em> and on the way <em>out</em>, and indent by the depth. The indentation is what makes the shape visible: each level steps right, and the returns line up with their matching entries.</p><p>Infinite recursion is instantly recognisable in that output — the same argument repeating, or the indentation marching right without a base case ever printing. Passing a <code>depth</code> parameter costs nothing and is the cheapest recursion debugger there is.</p><p>Trace with a small input. <code>fact(4)</code> produces readable output; <code>fact(40)</code> produces a wall of text that hides the very thing you are looking for.</p><i data-d286u811="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="callout" data-lb="why" style="border-left-color:#4f46e5;"><div class="callout-label">📘 DEFINITION</div><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Trace output:</strong> temporary prints showing entry, exit and arguments</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Depth parameter:</strong> an extra argument used only to indent the trace</p><p style="margin:0 0 7px;"><strong>Winding / unwinding:</strong> the descent to the base case and the return back up through the calls</p></div><div class="callout" data-lb="oa" style="border-left-color:#e11d48;"><div class="callout-label">🎯 EXAM TIP</div><p>In an exam, draw the call stack instead: one indented line per call, then fill in return values from the deepest line upward. It is the same diagram the prints would have produced.</p></div><i data-d286_z11_4="1" style="display:none"></i><div class="vl" data-mathvis="1" data-c959fig="1" style="margin-top:18px;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — print at both ends of the call</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 600 154" style="width:100%; max-width:600px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fk403a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker></defs><rect x="14" y="22" width="250" height="24" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="24" y="39" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">on entry</text><text x="280" y="39" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">the argument it received</text><rect x="14" y="52" width="250" height="24" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="24" y="69" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">on exit</text><text x="280" y="69" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">the value it returns</text><rect x="14" y="82" width="250" height="24" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="24" y="99" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">indent by depth</text><text x="280" y="99" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">shows the nesting</text><rect x="14" y="112" width="250" height="24" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="24" y="129" fill="var(--text)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace">remove them after</text><text x="280" y="129" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">or guard with a flag</text></svg></div></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — Tracing entry and exit</div><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; padding:11px 13px; overflow-x:auto; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0;">System.out.println(fib(4, 0));</pre><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--accent); background:var(--surface-2); padding:8px 12px; margin:8px 0 4px; font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap;">fib(4)
