3</div><div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-3); font-style:italic; margin-bottom:10px;">actual output, captured from the JVM</div><ol><li>Each line's indentation is its depth in the call tree.</li><li>You can see the same subproblem being solved more than once.</li><li>Printing on the way in AND on the way out is what makes the structure visible.</li></ol></div><div class="callout" data-lb="key" style="border-left-color:#0ea5e9;"><div class="callout-label">▸ WORKED EXAMPLE — Counting how often it recurses</div><pre style="background:var(--surface-2); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; padding:11px 13px; overflow-x:auto; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0;">calls = 0;
System.out.println(fib(10));
System.out.println(calls);
calls = 0;
System.out.println(fib(20));
System.out.println(calls);</pre><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--accent); background:var(--surface-2); padding:8px 12px; margin:8px 0 4px; font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap;">55
