<details class="vl-orig" open><summary>📖 Full cheat sheet — every reference table (tap to collapse)</summary><div>
<h3>Java Cheat Sheet — Unit 1: Basics, Types &amp; I/O</h3>
<p>JVM/JRE/JDK, the 8 primitive types, casting, operators, Strings, and Scanner input.</p>

<h4>① How Java runs</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Tool</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">What it is</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Use it to…</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">JVM</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">Java Virtual Machine — runs bytecode</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">execute (platform-independent)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">JRE</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">JVM + core libraries</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><strong>RUN</strong> Java apps</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">JDK</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">JRE + compiler (javac) + tools</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><strong>DEVELOP</strong> Java apps</td></tr>
</table>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>.java</strong> → (javac compiler) → <strong>.class bytecode</strong> → (JVM) → runs on any platform</div>
<pre style="background:var(--surface-2);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;margin:8px 0">public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, world!");
    }
}</pre>

<h4>② The 8 primitive types</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Type</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Size</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Holds</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Example</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">byte</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">8-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">whole −128..127</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">byte b = 100;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">short</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">16-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">whole</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">short s = 1000;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">int</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">32-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">whole (default)</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">int i = 42;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">long</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">64-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">big whole</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">long n = 90000000000L;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">float</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">32-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">decimal</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">float f = 3.14f;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">double</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">64-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">decimal (default)</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">double d = 3.14;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">char</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">16-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">one Unicode char</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">char c = 'A';</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">boolean</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">1-bit</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">true / false</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">boolean ok = true;</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Defaults: numbers 0 / 0.0, char null char, boolean false, objects null. A <code>long</code> literal needs <code>L</code>; a <code>float</code> literal needs <code>f</code>.</p>

<h4>③ Type casting &amp; division</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Conversion</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Rule</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Widening</span> (small → big)</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">Automatic and safe: int → long → double; char → int.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Narrowing</span> (big → small)</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">Needs an explicit cast: <code>int x = (int) 3.9;</code> → 3 (truncates).</td></tr>
</table>
<div class='callout callout-pitfall'><div class='callout-label'>⚠ INTEGER DIVISION</div>
<code>7 / 2 = 3</code> (int ÷ int truncates). For 3.5 use <code>7.0 / 2</code> or <code>(double) 7 / 2</code>. <code>7 % 2 = 1</code> (remainder). <code>char</code> is numeric: <code>'A' + 1 = 66</code>; <code>(char)('A' + 1) = 'B'</code>.</div>

<h4>④ Operators</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Group</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Operators</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Arithmetic</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">+ − * / % &nbsp;(% = remainder)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Relational</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">== != &lt; &gt; &lt;= &gt;= &nbsp;(result is boolean)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Logical</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">&amp;&amp; (and) · || (or) · ! (not) — short-circuit</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Assignment</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">= += −= *= /= %=</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">Increment</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">++ −−</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Precedence: <strong>*</strong> <strong>/</strong> <strong>%</strong> before <strong>+</strong> <strong>−</strong>; use parentheses to be safe.</p>

<h4>⑤ Strings</h4>
<ul>
<li><span class="key-term">String</span> is a reference type and <strong>immutable</strong>; build with <code>+</code> concatenation.</li>
<li>Compare CONTENT with <code>.equals()</code> — <strong>not</strong> <code>==</code> (which compares references).</li>
<li>Handy methods: <code>.length()</code>, <code>.charAt(i)</code>, <code>.substring(a, b)</code>, <code>.indexOf(x)</code>, <code>.toUpperCase()</code>, <code>.equalsIgnoreCase()</code>, <code>.trim()</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h4>⑥ Scanner (keyboard input)</h4>
<pre style="background:var(--surface-2);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;margin:8px 0">import java.util.Scanner;
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
int age = sc.nextInt();
double gpa = sc.nextDouble();
sc.nextLine();              // consume the leftover newline
String name = sc.nextLine();</pre>
<div class='callout callout-pitfall'><div class='callout-label'>⚠ COMMON TRAPS</div><ul>
<li><code>7 / 2 = 3</code> — integer division truncates.</li>
<li>Strings: <code>==</code> compares references; use <code>.equals()</code> for content.</li>
<li><code>array.length</code> (no parentheses) vs <code>str.length()</code> (method) vs <code>list.size()</code>.</li>
<li><code>nextInt()</code> / <code>nextDouble()</code> leave a newline — call <code>sc.nextLine()</code> before reading a full line.</li>
</ul></div>
<div class='callout callout-recall'><div class='callout-label'>✓ UNIT 1 MUST-KNOWS</div><ul>
<li>JDK develops · JRE runs · JVM executes bytecode (platform-independent).</li>
<li>8 primitives; int &amp; double are the defaults; long → L, float → f.</li>
<li>Widening is automatic; narrowing needs a cast and truncates.</li>
<li>Integer division truncates; % is remainder; char is numeric ('A' = 65).</li>
</ul></div>

<h3>➕ Expanded reference — outputs straight from the JVM</h3>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>Integer math — every value below was actually printed by Java</strong><br>
<table><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th><th>Why</th></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>7 / 2</td><td class='num'>3</td><td>int ÷ int truncates toward zero</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>-7 / 2</td><td class='num'>-3</td><td>truncation, not floor</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>7 % 3</td><td class='num'>1</td><td>remainder</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>-7 % 3</td><td class='num'>-1</td><td>result takes the LEFT operand's sign</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>7 / 2.0</td><td class='num'>3.5</td><td>one double makes it double division</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>(int) 3.9</td><td class='num'>3</td><td>cast truncates — never rounds</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1</td><td class='num'>-2147483648</td><td>silent overflow wraps to MIN_VALUE</td></tr></table></div>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>String + number — reads LEFT to RIGHT</strong><br>
<table><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>"1" + 2 + 3</td><td class='num'>"123" (string first → everything concatenates)</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>1 + 2 + "3"</td><td class='num'>"33" (adds 1+2 BEFORE meeting the string)</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>'A' + 1</td><td class='num'>66 (char promotes to int)</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>(char)('A' + 1)</td><td class='num'>'B'</td></tr></table></div>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>String methods on "Hello, World" (indexes start at 0)</strong><br>
<table><tr><th>Call</th><th>Result</th></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>.length()</td><td class='num'>12</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>.charAt(1)</td><td class='num'>'e'</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>.substring(7)</td><td class='num'>"World" (from index 7 to end)</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>.substring(0, 5)</td><td class='num'>"Hello" (end index EXCLUDED)</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>.indexOf("o")</td><td class='num'>4 (first hit only)</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>.toUpperCase()</td><td class='num'>"HELLO, WORLD" (returns NEW string — originals never change)</td></tr></table></div>
<div class='callout callout-recall'><div class='callout-label'>✓ == vs .equals() — VERIFIED</div><ul>
<li>"hi" == "hi" → true (same pooled literal) but new String("hi") == "hi" → false. .equals() → true both times.</li>
<li>Rule: ALWAYS compare strings with .equals(). == on objects compares addresses.</li>
<li>printf: %.2f → 3.14 · %5d right-aligns ("&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;42") · %-5d left-aligns ("42&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;") · %n = newline.</li>
<li>Integer.parseInt("42") → int 42 · String.valueOf(42) → "42".</li></ul></div>
</div></details>"},"D286/cheat/s2":{"body":"
