<details class="vl-orig" open><summary>📖 Full cheat sheet — every reference table (tap to collapse)</summary><div>
<h3>Java Cheat Sheet — Unit 2: Control Flow</h3>
<p>if/else, switch, the three loops, and break/continue.</p>

<h4>① if / else if / else</h4>
<pre style="background:var(--surface-2);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;margin:8px 0">if (score &gt;= 90) {
    grade = 'A';
} else if (score &gt;= 80) {
    grade = 'B';
} else {
    grade = 'F';
}</pre>

<h4>② switch</h4>
<p>Works on <code>int</code>, <code>char</code>, <code>String</code>, and <code>enum</code>. Each case needs <strong>break</strong> or it <strong>falls through</strong> to the next case.</p>
<pre style="background:var(--surface-2);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;margin:8px 0">switch (day) {
    case 1: System.out.println("Mon"); break;
    case 2: System.out.println("Tue"); break;
    default: System.out.println("Other");
}</pre>

<h4>③ The three loops</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Loop</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Checks the condition</th><th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface-2);font-weight:700">Use when</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">while</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">before the body (pretest)</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">unknown number of repeats</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">do-while</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">after the body (posttest)</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">must run <strong>at least once</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top"><span class="key-term">for</span></td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">before the body</td><td style="padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top">a known count</td></tr>
</table>
<pre style="background:var(--surface-2);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;margin:8px 0">for (int i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {        // runs i = 0,1,2,3,4
    System.out.println(i);
}

int n = 5;
while (n &gt; 0) { n--; }

do { x++; } while (x &lt; 3);          // body runs at least once

for (int v : numbers) {             // enhanced for (for-each)
    System.out.println(v);
}</pre>

<h4>④ break &amp; continue</h4>
<ul>
<li><code>break</code> — exit the loop (or switch case) immediately.</li>
<li><code>continue</code> — skip to the next iteration.</li>
</ul>
<div class='callout callout-pitfall'><div class='callout-label'>⚠ TRAPS</div><ul>
<li><code>do-while</code> always runs <strong>at least once</strong> (condition checked after the body).</li>
<li>A missing <code>break</code> in a switch makes execution <strong>fall through</strong> into later cases.</li>
<li>Off-by-one: <code>for (i = 0; i &lt; n; i++)</code> runs n times (0..n−1).</li>
</ul></div>
<div class='callout callout-recall'><div class='callout-label'>✓ UNIT 2 MUST-KNOWS</div><ul>
<li>while = pretest · do-while = posttest (≥ 1 run) · for = counted.</li>
<li>switch needs break to avoid fall-through; it supports String.</li>
<li>Enhanced for (for-each) reads each element; it has no index to change.</li>
</ul></div>

<h3>➕ Expanded reference — traced control flow (all outputs JVM-verified)</h3>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>Three loops, traced</strong><br>
<table><tr><th>Code</th><th>Prints</th><th>Lesson</th></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>for (int i = 0; i &lt; 5; i += 2)</td><td class='num'>0 2 4</td><td>test runs BEFORE each pass</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>int n=10; do { print(n); n++; } while (n &lt; 10);</td><td class='num'>10</td><td>do-while always runs at least once</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>while (n &lt; 10) with n=10</td><td class='num'>(nothing)</td><td>while can run zero times</td></tr></table></div>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>switch fallthrough — the most-missed trace question</strong><br>
day = 2, cases 1..4 where only case 3 has a break:<br>
<span class='num'>case 1: "Mon" · case 2: "Tue" · case 3: "Wed" break; · case 4: "Thu"</span><br>
Prints <strong>"Tue Wed"</strong> — enters at the matching case and FALLS THROUGH every case below it until a break.</div>
<div class='formula-box'><strong>Ternary &amp; short-circuit</strong><br>
<table><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>(5 % 2 == 0) ? "even" : "odd"</td><td class='num'>"odd"</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>false &amp;&amp; anything()</td><td class='num'>right side NEVER runs</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>true || anything()</td><td class='num'>right side NEVER runs</td></tr>
<tr><td class='num'>&amp; and | (single)</td><td class='num'>always evaluate BOTH sides</td></tr></table></div>
<div class='callout callout-recall'><div class='callout-label'>✓ TRACE-QUESTION HABITS</div><ul>
<li>Write the variable table: one column per variable, one row per loop pass. Never trace in your head.</li>
<li>break leaves the LOOP · continue skips to the NEXT pass (in a for loop, the update i++ still runs).</li>
<li>Off-by-one: i &lt; 5 runs for i = 0,1,2,3,4 (five times). i &lt;= 5 runs six times.</li></ul></div>
</div></details>"},"D286/cheat/s3":{"body":"
