  System.out.println(s[0]);","options":["""","null","empty","0"],"correct":1,"explain":"Object-type arrays default each element to null.","distractors":{"0":"An empty String "" is not the default — uninitialized object references are null.","2":"An empty String "" is not the default — uninitialized object references are null.","3":"An empty String "" is not the default — uninitialized object references are null."},"_practice":true,"__rebal":1}],"D286/cheat/s3":[{"id":"g14","topic":"this","text":"The keyword this refers to:","options":["a static field","the current object","the JVM","the parent class"],"correct":1,"explain":"this is a reference to the current object.","__rebal":1},{"id":"i13","topic":"static cannot","text":"A static method cannot:","options":["be called without creating an object first","directly access an instance field or use this","be overloaded with different parameter lists","return a value of a reference type"],"correct":1,"explain":"With no object, a static method has no this and no instance fields.","__rebal":1},{"id":"tuw1_d286_u5_2","topic":"Inner class access","text":"A (non-static) inner class can access the enclosing object’s:","options":["Nothing","Only public methods","Only static members","Private instance fields and methods"],"correct":3,"explain":"An inner class is tied to an outer instance and can access all its members, including private ones."},{"id":"px286_encap_2","topic":"Which access modifier makes a field visible ONLY","text":"Which access modifier makes a field visible ONLY within its own class?","options":["private","protected","default (package)","public"],"correct":0,"explain":"private restricts access to the declaring class alone.","distractors":{"0":"protected allows access from subclasses and the same package — broader than private.","1":"protected allows access from subclasses and the same package — broader than private.","3":"protected allows access from subclasses and the same package — broader than private."},"_pr