"medium"},{"id":"zf861","topic":"","text":"The binary number 100000 equals which decimal value?","options":["16","64","100","32"],"correct":3,"explain":"A single 1 in the sixth position from the right is the 32s place.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf862","topic":"","text":"How many bits does the decimal number 9 need in binary?","options":["4 (1001)","3","9","2"],"correct":0,"explain":"9 = 8 + 1 = 1001 in binary - four bits.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u2/z2_16":[{"id":"zya2_16_0","topic":"Overflow behaviour","text":"What happens when an int exceeds Integer.MAX_VALUE?","options":["It converts to long","An exception is thrown","It wraps around to negative values","It saturates at MAX_VALUE"],"correct":2,"explain":"Java integer arithmetic wraps silently. Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1 equals Integer.MIN_VALUE — no warning at all."},{"id":"zya2_16_1","topic":"int max value","text":"Integer.MAX_VALUE is approximately:","options":["65,535","32,767","2.1 billion","9.2 quintillion"],"correct":2,"explain":"2^31 - 1 = 2,147,483,647. Beyond that you need long."},{"id":"zya2_16_2","topic":"Avoiding overflow","text":"A calculation may exceed int range. The correct fix is:","options":["Catch the exception","Add a comment","Use long instead of int","Use double for exactness"],"correct":2,"explain":"long holds about 9.2 quintillion. Catching does not work because no exception is thrown."},{"id":"zya2_16_3","topic":"Overflow in an expression","text":"int a = 2000000000; int b = a + a; What is b?","options":["A compile error","4000000000","A negative number","Integer.MAX_VALUE"],"correct":2,"explain":"The sum exceeds int range and wraps to a negative value — a classic silent bug."},{"id":"zya2_16_4","topic":"Promoting before overflow","text":"Which avoids overflow when multiplying two large ints a and b?","options":["double r = a * b;","long r = a * b;","long r = (long) a * b;","long r = (long)(a * b);"],"correct":2,"explain":"Cast one operand first so the multiplication itself is done 