System.out.println("Result: " + (10 > 20 ? "yes" : "no"));","options":["Compiler error","Result: no","Result: yes","Result: false"],"correct":1,"explain":"Because the ternary is an expression, it can sit inside a println argument. 10 > 20 is false, so it produces "no", which is concatenated after "Result: ". The parentheses around the ternary are what keep the concatenation from grabbing the condition first."},{"id":"fs_z3_17_3","topic":"Ternary with arithmetic branches","text":"What does this print?

