":"","text":"for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) System.out.print("ab"); prints:","options":["ab ab ab","abc","ababab","ab"],"correct":2,"explain":"The two-letter string prints three times with nothing between.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf658","topic":"","text":"The average of the ints 4, 7, 9 computed with a loop and count is:","options":["20 / 3 as ints, giving 6, is always right","the middle value 7","the last value 9","sum / count with doubles - 20 / 3.0 gives about 6.67"],"correct":3,"explain":"Averaging needs floating division; int division would drop the fraction.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u4/z4_6":[{"id":"zya4_6_0","topic":"Looping over characters","text":"To visit every character of String s:","options":["for (int i=0; i<=s.length(); i++)","for (int i=0; i<s.length(); i++)","for (int i=1; i<s.length(); i++)","for (char c : s)"],"correct":1,"explain":"Indices run 0 to length-1. Using <= throws StringIndexOutOfBoundsException, and a String is not directly iterable."},{"id":"zya4_6_1","topic":"Char at index","text":"Inside such a loop, the character is obtained with:","options":["s[i]","s.charAt(i)","s.get(i)","s.substring(i)"],"correct":1,"explain":"Strings use charAt; bracket indexing works only on arrays."},{"id":"zya4_6_2","topic":"Counting a character","text":"To count how many times 'a' appears in s:","options":["if (s.charAt(i) = 'a') count++;","if (s.charAt(i) == 'a') count++;","if (s.charAt(i).equals('a')) count++;","count += s.charAt(i);"],"correct":1,"explain":"char is a primitive, so == is correct and equals does not apply."},{"id":"zya4_6_3","topic":"Building a reversed String","text":"String r = ""; for (int i=s.length()-1; i>=0; i--) r += s.charAt(i); produces:","options":["The original String","The reverse of s","An empty String","A compile error"],"correct":1,"explain":"Walking backwards and appending builds the reverse. For long Strings a StringBuilder avoids the repeated copying."},{"id":"zy4_6_1_lg_D286_0_68","topic":"Performance","text":"Building a long string inside a loop is best done with:","options":["StringBuilder.append","+= on String","String.concat","char math"],"correct":0,"explain":"Strings are immutable; += copies every pass. StringBuilder mutates one buffer.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy4_6_3_bp_D286_t12_11","topic":"Reverse string","text":"To reverse a string with a loop you iterate:","options":["from 0 up to length-1, appending charAt(i)","from length-1 down to 0, appending charAt(i)","from length down to 1, appending charAt(i)","from 0 up to length/2, swapping charAt(i)"],"correct":1,"explain":"Walk backward from the last index, appending each char.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zyf4_6_0","topic":"Vowel counting","text":"Counting vowels in a String requires comparing each char against:","options":["Only the first vowel found in the string","The ASCII range between 'a' and 'u' inclusive","All five vowels, with contains or a multi-way condition","The string's length divided by five"],"correct":2,"explain":""aeiou".indexOf(c) >= 0 is the compact form."},{"id":"zyf4_6_1","topic":"toCharArray","text":"for (char c : s.toCharArray()) is:","options":["A valid way to iterate a String without indices","A compile error, since String is not an array","A loop that visits only the first character","A loop that requires an explicit index variable"],"correct":0,"explain":"It builds an array first, then uses the enhanced for."},{"id":"fs_z4_6_1","topic":"Counting characters","text":"What does this print?

