ilds "012" - not arithmetic.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf665","topic":"","text":"int spaces = 0; String s6 = "a b c"; for (int i = 0; i < s6.length(); i++) if (s6.charAt(i) == ' ') spaces++; System.out.println(spaces); prints:","options":["1","2","3","5"],"correct":1,"explain":"The 5-character string has spaces at indexes 1 and 3.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf666","topic":"","text":"Building a string in a loop with + works but for heavy work Java offers:","options":["StringCollector","charAt in reverse","StringBuilder with append","the += operator only"],"correct":2,"explain":"Each + makes a new string; StringBuilder appends in place efficiently.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf667","topic":"","text":"String dup = ""; String base6 = "ha"; for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) dup += base6; System.out.println(dup.length()); prints:","options":["3","2","8","6"],"correct":3,"explain":""hahaha" - three copies of a 2-character string.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf668","topic":"","text":"Checking whether "level" reads the same reversed requires comparing:","options":["charAt(i) with charAt(length","only the first and last letters","the lengths of both halves","the middle letter to itself"],"correct":0,"explain":"The palindrome test pairs characters from both ends walking inward.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf669","topic":"","text":"int digits6 = 0; String id6 = "a1b22"; for (int i = 0; i < id6.length(); i++) if (Character.isDigit(id6.charAt(i))) digits6++; System.out.println(digits6); prints:","options":["2","3","4","5"],"correct":1,"explain":"The digits are 1, 2, 2 - three of the five characters.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u4/z4_7":[{"id":"zya4_7_0","topic":"Total iterations","text":"for (i=0;i&lt;3;i++) for (j=0;j&lt;4;j++) — the inner body runs:","options":["4 times","7 times","12 times","3 times"],"correct":2,"explain":"Outer count times inner count. This multiplication is why nested loops are O(n^2)."},{"id":"zya4_7_1","topic":"Inner loop restart","text":"The inner loop's counter:","options":["Cannot be changed","Keeps its value across outer iterations","Is reinitialized each time the outer loop repeats","Is shared with the outer loop"],"correct":2,"explain":"Its initialization runs on every entry to the inner loop."},{"id":"zya4_7_2","topic":"Triangle pattern","text":"for (i=1;i&lt;=3;i++){ for(j=1;j&lt;=i;j++) print("*"); println(); } prints:","options":["A right triangle of 1, 2, then 3 stars","A square of three rows of three stars","An inverted triangle of 3, 2, then 1 stars","A single row of six stars with no line breaks"],"correct":0,"explain":"The inner bound depends on i, which is how nested loops draw shapes."},{"id":"zya4_7_3","topic":"Rows and columns","text":"For a 2D array, the outer loop usually iterates over:","options":["Nothing","Columns","Rows","Elements"],"correct":2,"explain":"Outer over rows, inner over columns, matching a[row][col]."},{"id":"zya4_7_4","topic":"Nested loop cost","text":"Nesting two loops over n items gives complexity:","options":["O(n)","O(2n)","O(n^2)","O(log n)"],"correct":2,"explain":"Which is why a nested loop over a large array becomes slow very quickly."},{"id":"zy4_7_2_q6","topic":"2D traversal","text":"Inner loop condition for 2D array traversal should use:","options":["constant 10","grid.length","grid[r].length","grid[0].length only"],"correct":2,"explain":"grid[r].length gives number of columns in row r. Handles jagged arrays.","distractors":{"0":"Hardcoded constants break for different sizes.","2":"grid.length = rows; inner needs columns.","3":"grid[0].length works for rectangular but grid[r].length is more general."},"__rebal":1},{"id":"zy4_7_3_k14","topic":"Inner bound","text":"The inner loop bound for traversing 2D array grid should use:","options":["grid.length","r","grid[0]","grid[r].length"],"correct":3,"explain":"Use the current row’s length: grid[r].length.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy4_7_4_h6_286_9","topic":"nested loop output","_dom":"control","difficulty":"hard",