g back x * x","stores x * x in a field","restarts the method"],"correct":1,"explain":"return supplies the caller’s value and exits immediately.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2008","topic":"","text":"int r = add(2, 4); The returned value:","options":["is printed automatically","is discarded","is stored in r","replaces the method"],"correct":2,"explain":"The call expression evaluates to the return value, which the assignment captures.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2009","topic":"","text":"Code after a return statement in the same block:","options":["runs next call","runs once","runs twice","never runs (unreachable)"],"correct":3,"explain":"return exits the method; the compiler even rejects clearly unreachable code.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2010","topic":"","text":"A method may have how many parameters?","options":["exactly one","at most two","at least one","zero or more"],"correct":3,"explain":"Empty parentheses are fine; so are several comma-separated parameters.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2011","topic":"","text":"Calling add(2, 4) + add(1, 1) evaluates to:","options":["8","6","24","error"],"correct":0,"explain":"Method calls are expressions: 6 + 2 = 8.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zr5","topic":"User-defined method basics","text":"A method is declared as: static int twice(int n). What must its body do?","options":["print an int value and return nothing","return an int value","accept two int parameters","be called exactly twice"],"correct":1,"explain":"The return type in the header is a promise: a method declared int must return an int on every path. Printing is not returning.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zr6","topic":"User-defined method basics","text":"What does the word static mean in the header static double area(double r)?","options":["Its return value can never change once first computed","It may only be called once per program run, then it is fixed","It belongs to the class, so no object is needed to call it","Its parameter r is passed by reference rather than by value"],"correct":2,"explain":"A static method is called on the class itself, such as MathUtil.area(2.0). Non-static methods need an object first.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u6/z6_2":[{"id":"zy6_2_1_px286_static_7","topic":"What is printed","text":"What is printed?
