ach the caller","neither reaches the caller","both are compile errors"],"correct":0,"explain":"Shared object, private reference copy - the key rule of reference parameters.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2106","topic":"","text":"static double avgArr(int[] a) { int s = 0; for (int x : a) s += x; return (double) s / a.length; } avgArr(new int[]{3, 4}) returns:","options":["3","3.5","3.0","7.0"],"correct":1,"explain":"7 / 2.0 = 3.5; the cast makes the division floating point.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2107","topic":"","text":"Passing an array of 1,000,000 elements to a method copies:","options":["all million elements","half the elements","just the small reference","nothing at all"],"correct":2,"explain":"Reference passing is why big-array parameters are cheap.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2108","topic":"","text":"static boolean containsZero(int[] a) { for (int x : a) if (x == 0) return true; return false; } containsZero(new int[]{5, 0, 2}) returns:","options":["false","0","1","true"],"correct":3,"explain":"The scan hits the 0 at index 1.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2109","topic":"","text":"A method that should NOT change the caller’s array must:","options":["not write elements (or use a copy)","declare the parameter final","take an int instead","return void"],"correct":0,"explain":"Nothing stops element writes automatically - discipline (or copying) does. (final only stops reassignment.)","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2110","topic":"","text":"static void fillWith(int[] a, int val) { for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = val; } After fillWith(nums, 9) on a 3-element array, nums holds:","options":["9, 9, 9","its old values","9 only at index 0","nothing"],"correct":0,"explain":"Every slot was overwritten through the shared reference.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u6/z6_11":[{"id":"zy6_11_2_z286_oo4","topic":"private","_dom":"oop","text":"Which access modifier makes a member visible ONLY within its own class?","options":["private","default (package)","protected","public"],"correct":0,"explain":"private restricts access to the declaring class.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy6_11_3_q6","topic":"Local class","text":"Where is a local class visible?","options":["Throughout the enclosing class, like a field","Anywhere in the package that declares it","Only within the method where it is declared","Only inside the constructor of the outer class"],"correct":2,"explain":"A local class is declared inside a method and is only visible within that method.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy6_11_4_tuw1_d286_u5_8","topic":"Capturing variables","text":"An anonymous or local class can capture a local variable only if that variable is:","options":["Public","Volatile","Static","Effectively final"],"correct":3,"explain":"Captured local variables must be final or effectively final (never reassigned after initialization)."},{"id":"zyf6_11_0","topic":"Method-local scope","text":"A variable declared in one method is visible in another:","options":["Only in main","Yes","No","Only if static"],"correct":2,"explain":"Sharing requires a parameter, a return value, or a field. Locals are confined to their own method."},{"id":"zyf6_11_1","topic":"Field visibility","text":"A field declared in a class is visible:","options":["Throughout the class, in every method","Only inside the method that first assigns it","Only within the block where it is declared","Anywhere in the package that declares the class"],"correct":0,"explain":"Which is how methods share state."},{"id":"zyf6_11_2","topic":"Shadowing a field","text":"A local variable with the same name as a field:","options":["Is a compile error; the names must be distinct","Silently overwrites the field's stored value","Shadows the field; use this.name to reach the field","Refers to the field, since fields take precedence"],"correct":2,"explain":"Constructors rely on this.name = name for exactly this reason."},{"id":"zyf6_11_3","topic":"Parameter scope","text":"A parameter is in scope:","options":["After the return","Everywhere in the class","For the whole method body","Only on the first line"],"correct":2,"explain":"It behaves like a local initialized from the argument."},{"id":"fs_z6_11_1","topic":"Locals are invisible to other methods","text":"static void a() {
