rmost block wins - loop headers make loop-local variables.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2120","topic":"","text":"Which data should become a parameter rather than a field?","options":["a true constant","a value that differs per call","the class name","nothing"],"correct":1,"explain":"Per-call inputs belong in the signature; shared fixed state can be a field or constant.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2121","topic":"","text":"Calling a method never gives it access to:","options":["its own parameters","its own locals","the caller’s local variables","class-level constants"],"correct":2,"explain":"Only what is passed in (or class-scoped) is visible - main’s locals stay private to main.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zj11","topic":"Scope","text":"A variable declared inside a method body can be used:","options":["anywhere in the class that declares the method","in any method of any class in the program","only inside that method, after its declaration","only if it is also declared in main"],"correct":2,"explain":"A local variable's scope runs from its declaration to the closing brace of the block it sits in. Outside that block the name is not visible at all.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u6/z6_12":[{"id":"zy6_12_3_i17","topic":"Resolution","text":"Overloading is resolved:","options":["at compile time","by the JVM only","never","at runtime"],"correct":0,"explain":"The compiler picks the overload based on argument types at compile time.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy6_12_4_px286_static_1","topic":"What is method overloading","text":"What is method overloading?","options":["A method that calls itself","Two methods with the same name but different parameter lists","A method with no return type","Redefining a parent method in a child class"],"correct":1,"explain":"Overloading = same method name, different parameters (number or types).","distractors":{"1":"Redefining a parent method in a child is OVERRIDING, not overloading.","2":"Redefining a parent method in a child is OVERRIDI