ned, since everything is in one place","Cannot compile without being split into three","Runs faster than three collaborating classes","Is doing too much and is hard to test or reuse"],"correct":3,"explain":"Separate concerns so each part can change independently."},{"id":"zya7_6_4","topic":"When not to make a class","text":"A single value with no associated behaviour:","options":["Can just be a variable","Must be static","Needs inheritance","Always needs a class"],"correct":0,"explain":"Wrapping an int in a class with a getter and nothing else adds ceremony without benefit."},{"id":"zya7_6_5","topic":"Methods from verbs","text":""A library lends books" suggests:","options":["A lend method on Library","A lend field","No methods","A Lend class"],"correct":0,"explain":"Actions become methods on the class that owns the relevant data."},{"id":"zya7_6_6","topic":"Object identity","text":"Two Student objects with identical field values are:","options":["Distinct objects, equal in content only if equals is overridden","The same object, since Java interns identical values","Always equal under ==, because the fields match","A compile error, since duplicates are not permitted"],"correct":0,"explain":"Identity is reference-based unless you override equals."},{"id":"zy7_6_2_lg_D286_0_6","topic":"Reading input","text":"Which class reads keyboard input in Java?","options":["BufferedImage","Scanner","Reader","Printer"],"correct":1,"explain":"Scanner (often new Scanner(System.in)) reads user input.","__rebal":1},{"id":"fs_z7_6_1","topic":"Nouns, verbs and adjectives","text":"Consider this description: "A hotel books rooms for guests. Each room has a number and a nightly rate." Which item is the strongest candidate to become a FIELD rather than a class or a method?","options":["Guest","Room","book","nightlyRate"],"correct":3,"explain":"Adjectives and descriptive values become fields, nouns become classes and verbs become methods. nightlyRate describes a Room, so it is one of Room's fields."},{"id":"fs_z7_6_2","topic":"Parallel arrays signal a class","text":"You keep String[] names and double[] balances aligned by index, and now you must sort by balance without breaking the pairing. What does that difficulty signal?","options":["The two arrays should be merged into one 2-D array","A name and a balance always travel together","The sort should be moved into a static method","The arrays should be replaced by two ArrayLists"],"correct":1,"explain":"Two arrays that must be kept in step by hand are a class waiting to be written: put the paired values in one object and they cannot drift apart. An ArrayList or a 2-D array keeps the same alignment problem. They belong in one Account class."},{"id":"fs_z7_6_3","topic":"Has-a relationship","text":"A Course class holds an Instructor object as one of its fields. This design is described as:","options":["a static relationship","an is-a relationship","a has-a relationship","constructor overloading"],"correct":2,"explain":"A class holding another class as a field models has-a: a Course has an Instructor. is-a describes inheritance, where one class is a kind of another."},{"id":"fs_z7_6_4","topic":"One class instead of parallel arrays","text":"Book stores a title and a price, with getTitle() and getPrice() accessors. What does this print?

