Student b = a;
b.setScore(50);
System.out.println(a.getScore() + " " + b.getScore());","options":["50 95","95 95","50 50","95 50"],"correct":2,"explain":"Student b = a; copies the reference, so there was only ever one object. Changing the score through b is visible through a because both names point at the same heap object."},{"id":"fs_z7_10_2","topic":"== and the inherited equals","text":"Student stores a name and a score and does NOT override equals. What does this print?

