true","true
false"],"correct":0,"explain":"Two new calls make two distinct objects, so == is false. The equals inherited from Object also compares references, so it behaves exactly like == until the class overrides it to compare field values."},{"id":"fs_z7_10_3","topic":"Default toString output","text":"A class that does not override toString() is handed to System.out.println. What appears?","options":["null","The class name, an @ sign, and a hexadecimal hash code","The values of all the object's fields, separated by commas","The object's memory address in decimal"],"correct":1,"explain":"println calls toString(), and the version inherited from Object produces text such as Student@1b6d. Seeing that output is the usual sign that the class has not defined toString itself."},{"id":"fs_z7_10_4","topic":"Default value of a reference field","text":"Locker declares a String field owner and an int field number, neither given an initial value, plus accessors for both. What does this print?

