 character","everything typed ever"],"correct":0,"explain":"Token-by-token consumption is how sequential reads compose.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2551","topic":"","text":"print writes to the stream WITHOUT:","options":["any characters","a newline","buffering","text"],"correct":1,"explain":"println = print + line terminator.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2552","topic":"","text":"Output can be redirected (e.g., java Prog > out.txt) because:","options":["Java detects files","println has a file mode","programs just write to out","it cannot"],"correct":2,"explain":"The OS re-aims the stream; the program is oblivious.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2553","topic":"","text":"The flow for reading a number: keyboard -> System.in -> Scanner ->:","options":["the screen","a file","the heap only","your int variable"],"correct":3,"explain":"Raw bytes to parsed value to variable - the full input pipeline.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2554","topic":"","text":"Mixing sc.nextInt() with a later sc.nextLine() surprises because:","options":["the number’s newline is still queued","Scanners reset","ints eat lines","nothing surprising"],"correct":0,"explain":"The leftover terminator is the most common intro-Java input bug.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2555","topic":"","text":"Closing a stream signals:","options":["the program crashed","no more data will flow","data reversal","a retry"],"correct":1,"explain":"Files especially need the close to flush and free handles.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2556","topic":"","text":"Which pairing is right for standard streams?","options":["in = errors","out = input","in = input; out = output; err = errors","err = files"],"correct":2,"explain":"The three standard streams and their roles.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u9/z9_3":[{"id":"zya9_3_0","topic":"StringBuilder purpose","text":"StringBuilder exists because:","options":["String cannot hold more than a fixed number of chars","String comparison with equals is unreliable","String concatenation in a loop creates a new String each time","String is not available before Java 8"],"correct":2,"explain":"Repeated += is O(n^2); StringBuilder append is amortized O(1)."},{"id":"zya9_3_1","topic":"Appending","text":"sb.append("x") does what?","options":["Returns a new StringBuilder only","Modifies the builder in place","Throws","Creates a String"],"correct":1,"explain":"StringBuilder is mutable, unlike String."},{"id":"zya9_3_2","topic":"Getting the result","text":"To obtain the finished text:","options":["sb.getString()","sb.toString()","sb.value()","(String) sb"],"correct":1,"explain":"toString produces the immutable String."},{"id":"zya9_3_3","topic":"Scanner on a String","text":"new Scanner("10 20 30") lets you:","options":["Read from the keyboard","Parse tokens from that String","Write to a String","Sort the String"],"correct":1,"explain":"The same Scanner API works over any source, which makes parsing testable."},{"id":"zya9_3_4","topic":"split","text":""a,b,c".split(",") returns:","options":["A String","An array of three Strings","A list","A char array"],"correct":1,"explain":"A very common way to parse CSV-style input."},{"id":"zya9_3_5","topic":"String immutability","text":"s.concat("x") without assignment:","options":["Appends x to s, changing it in place","Leaves s unchanged, returning a new String","Fails to compile without an assignment","Throws an exception because s is immutable"],"correct":1,"explain":"Every String method returns a new String rather than modifying the original."},{"id":"zya9_3_6","topic":"StringBuilder capacity","text":"StringBuilder grows:","options":["Never","Automatically as needed","Only to 16 characters","Only with a parameter"],"correct":1,"explain":"Same amortized growth strategy as ArrayList."},{"id":"zy9_3_0_h3_286_11","topic":"StringBuilder mutability","_dom":"oop","difficulty":"hard","text":"StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("ab"); sb.append("c"); System.out.println(sb); prints:","options":["ab","c","error","abc"],"correct":3,"explain":"StringBuilder is mutable, so append modifies it in place → "abc" (unlike String, which is immutable).","__rebal":1},{"id":"fs_z9_3_1","topic":"Scanner over a String","text":"What does this program print?

