nners are perfect for TESTING input code because:","options":["strings are faster","keyboards are rare","no typing is needed","they are not"],"correct":2,"explain":"Deterministic, repeatable input drives automated tests.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2570","topic":"","text":"Parsing one CSV-like line "Ana,90" typically uses:","options":["nextInt directly","charAt alone","line.split(",") producing the parts","printf"],"correct":2,"explain":"Split by the delimiter, then convert each piece.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2571","topic":"","text":"After String[] parts = "Ana,90".split(","); parts[1] is:","options":["the int 90",""Ana"","a char",""90" - still a String"],"correct":3,"explain":"split yields text; Integer.parseInt finishes the job.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2572","topic":"","text":"StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(); sb.append("a"); sb.append(5); sb.toString() is:","options":[""a5"",""a 5"",""5a"","an error"],"correct":0,"explain":"Appends accumulate in order; toString exports the result.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2573","topic":"","text":"StringBuilder beats repeated String + in loops because:","options":["it is prettier","it appends in place","+ is illegal in loops","it sorts output"],"correct":1,"explain":"Output assembled over many steps belongs in a builder.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2574","topic":"","text":"An output stream to a String (via StringBuilder or StringWriter) lets a program:","options":["skip output","print twice","build the report in memory first","avoid strings"],"correct":2,"explain":"Compose first, emit once - and tests can inspect the built text.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2575","topic":"","text":"Scanner lineScanner = new Scanner(scoreLine); inside a loop over lines:","options":["re-reads the file","conflicts with itself","is illegal","parses each line’s tokens independently"],"correct":3,"explain":"The line-then-tokens pattern: outer reader per line, inner scanner per line’s fields.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2576","topic":"","text":"sc.hasNextInt() on a String scanner positioned at "end":","options":["returns false","returns true","throws","returns 0"],"correct":0,"explain":""end" is not an int token - the has-check reports honestly.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2577","topic":"","text":"The unifying idea of this section is:","options":["strings replace files entirely","strings can be stream endpoints","streams are only console","printing is obsolete"],"correct":1,"explain":"Same stream interfaces, in-memory endpoints - powerful for testing and assembly.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u9/z9_4":[{"id":"zya9_4_0","topic":"Reading a file","text":"Reading a text file commonly uses:","options":["new Scanner(new File("data.txt"))","new File().read()","System.out","new Scanner(System.in)"],"correct":0,"explain":"Same Scanner API, different source."},{"id":"zya9_4_1","topic":"Checked exception","text":"FileNotFoundException is:","options":["Checked","A compile warning","An Error","Unchecked"],"correct":0,"explain":"The compiler enforces handling, unlike NumberFormatException. You must catch it or declare throws."},{"id":"zya9_4_2","topic":"Reading line by line","text":"The standard loop is:","options":["while (in.hasNextLine()) in.nextLine();","for (int i=0;i<n;i++)","while (true)","while (in.hasNext()) in.nextInt();"],"correct":0,"explain":"hasNextLine guards nextLine so it never runs past the end."},{"id":"zya9_4_3","topic":"try-with-resources","text":"try (Scanner in = new Scanner(f)) { ... } does what?","options":["Opens the Scanner but leaves closing to you","Retries the block if an exception is thrown","Catches every exception the block can throw","Closes the Scanner automatically however the block exits"],"correct":3,"explain":"Closing on the exception path is exactly what is easy to forget manually."},{"id":"zya9_4_4","topic":"Relative path","text":"A relative filename is resolved from:","options":["The directory holding the .class file","The user's 