System.out.println(n + " " + in.hasNextLine());","options":["3 false","3 true","2 false","4 false"],"correct":0,"explain":"hasNextLine() reports whether another line remains, so the loop consumes all three lines and then stops. This is the same loop shape used to read a file to its end."},{"id":"fs_z9_4_2","topic":"Reading past the end","text":"A program calls in.nextLine() when the file has already been read to its end. What happens?","options":["nextLine() returns null","nextLine() returns an empty String","The Scanner reopens the file and reads it again from the start","A NoSuchElementException is thrown"],"correct":3,"explain":"nextLine() with nothing left throws NoSuchElementException, which is why the standard loop asks hasNextLine() first. The same pairing applies to hasNextInt and nextInt."},{"id":"fs_z9_4_3","topic":"try-with-resources","text":"In try (Scanner in = new Scanner(new File("data.txt"))) { ... } catch (FileNotFoundException e) { ... }, when is the Scanner closed?","options":["When the garbage collector next reclaims the Scanner object","Automatically, before the catch block runs","Automatically, but only after the catch block finishes","Only if the program calls in.close() inside the try block"],"correct":1,"explain":"A resource declared in the try parentheses is closed as the try block is left, and that happens before any matching catch or finally runs. That ordering is why this form is preferred to closing by hand."},{"id":"fs_z9_4_4","topic":"Checked exceptions","text":"A method body contains Scanner in = new Scanner(new File("data.txt")); and nothing else. Why will the class not compile?","options":["A Scanner may only be constructed from System.in","The File object must be opened with open() before a Scanner can use it","A relative path is not allowed in a File constructor","FileNotFoundException is checked"],"correct":3,"explain":"The compiler refuses code that neither handles nor declares a checked exception. That is the difference from unchecked failures such as ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException, which need no declaration. It must be caught or declared with throws."},{"id":"fs_z9_4_5","topic":"Mixing nextInt and nextLine","text":"What does this program print?

