ss blocks subclassing.","__rebal":1},{"id":"n22","topic":"Constructors","text":"Constructors are:","options":["inherited","optional","not inherited by subclasses","always static"],"correct":2,"explain":"Constructors are not inherited; subclasses call them via super.","__rebal":1},{"id":"n23","topic":"super placement","text":"super(...) must appear:","options":["as the last statement of the constructor","anywhere inside the constructor body","outside the constructor, at class level","as the first statement of the constructor"],"correct":3,"explain":"super(...) must be the first statement.","__rebal":1},{"id":"px286_inh_1","topic":"Which keyword makes class  Dog  inherit from cla","text":"Which keyword makes class  Dog  inherit from class  Animal ?","options":["Dog inherits Animal","Dog extends Animal","Dog : Animal","Dog implements Animal"],"correct":1,"explain":"A class inherits from another using extends: class Dog extends Animal.","distractors":{"0":"implements is for interfaces; extends is for class inheritance.","2":"implements is for interfaces; extends is for class inheritance.","3":"implements is for interfaces; extends is for class inheritance."},"_practice":true,"__rebal":1},{"id":"px286_inh_3","topic":"How many classes can a Java class directly  exte","text":"How many classes can a Java class directly  extend ?","options":["Up to two","Unlimited","Zero","Exactly one"],"correct":3,"explain":"Java supports single inheritance — a class extends at most one superclass.","distractors":{"0":"Multiple inheritance of classes is not allowed; only interfaces can be multiply implemented.","2":"Multiple inheritance of classes is not allowed; only interfaces can be multiply implemented.","3":"Multiple inheritance of classes is not allowed; only interfaces can be multiply implemented."},"_practice":true,"__rebal":1},{"id":"z2_in1","topic":"final class","_dom":"inherit","text":"In Java, a class declared with which keyword cannot be subclassed (extended)?","options":["private","abstract","final","static"],"correct":2,"explain":"A final class cannot be extended.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zf4001","topic":"","text":"class Truck extends Vehicle { } Here Truck is:","options":["the base class","the derived (sub) class","an interface","an object"],"correct":1,"explain":"extends names the base; the new class is the derived one.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4002","topic":"","text":"A derived class inherits from its base:","options":["nothing","only constructors","the accessible fields and methods","only private members"],"correct":2,"explain":"Public/protected members carry down; constructors are not inherited.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4003","topic":"","text":"The main purpose of inheritance is:","options":["faster loops","hiding all methods","removing objects","reusing and extending existing classes"],"correct":3,"explain":"Model "a Truck IS a Vehicle plus extras" without rewriting Vehicle.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4004","topic":"","text":"A derived class may add:","options":["new fields and methods of its own","nothing new","only comments","only constructors"],"correct":0,"explain":"Extension is the point: everything inherited plus the new members.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zr9","topic":"Derived classes","text":"class Car extends Vehicle. Which statement is true?","options":["Vehicle inherits Car's members","Car inherits Vehicle's public members and may add its own","Car must redefine every method Vehicle declares","Car and Vehicle each get a separate copy of the program"],"correct":1,"explain":"The derived class extends the base: it receives the base class's accessible members and can add to or override them. Inheritance only flows downward.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zy4_8_4_q8","topic":"final class","text":"final class BankAccount. Developer writes class SecureBankAccount extends BankAccount. Result?","options":["Works normally","Compile error","Works with cast","Works if SecureBankAccount also final"],"correct":1