":"","text":"A derived class in the SAME file/package as its base still cannot touch:","options":["public members","the base’s private members directly","protected members","static constants"],"correct":1,"explain":"private is class-private, not family-private.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4015","topic":"","text":"Choosing protected over private for a base field is justified when:","options":["always","never","subclasses genuinely need direct access","the field is unused"],"correct":2,"explain":"Default to private; loosen deliberately, not habitually.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u10/z10_3":[{"id":"zy10_3_5_q12","topic":"@Override benefit","text":"Why add @Override above equals()?","options":["It makes the equals() method run faster at execution time","The compiler verifies you overrode a method rather than overloaded","It generates the matching hashCode() method for you","It is required, or equals() will never actually be called"],"correct":1,"explain":"@Override makes the compiler error out if the method doesn't match an inherited one — catching the equals(Object) signature slip.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy10_3_6_lg_D286_0_56","topic":"Override","text":"Overriding means:","options":["Creating an interface","A subclass redefines a parent’s method","Same name, different parameters","Hiding a field"],"correct":1,"explain":"An override replaces the inherited implementation with the same signature.","__rebal":1},{"id":"q6","topic":"Override vs overload","text":"Parent has void print(int x). Child has void print(String s). Is this overriding?","options":["Yes — the method names match, which is what matters","No — a different parameter type makes it overloading","Yes, but only if @Override is written above it","No — overriding also requires a different return type"],"correct":1,"explain":"Overriding requires identical signatures. Different parameter type = overloading.","__rebal":1},{"id":"h3_286_9","topic":"overriding return","_dom":"inherit","difficulty":"hard","text":"A subclass method has the SAME name and parameters as the parent's but a different return type only. This is:","options":["a valid override, since the signature matches","a valid overload, since the return type differs","a compile error (not a valid override or overload)","a runtime error thrown when the method is called"],"correct":2,"explain":"Overriding requires a compatible return type; changing ONLY the return type is neither a valid override nor an overload → compile error.","__rebal":1},{"id":"q6_d2","topic":"equals signature","text":"What is the correct signature to OVERRIDE equals?","options":["public boolean equals(Point p)","public void equals(Object o)","public int equals(Object o)","public boolean equals(Object o)"],"correct":3,"explain":"Overriding requires the exact inherited signature: public boolean equals(Object o). A different parameter type only overloads.","distractors":{"0":"Parameter must be Object, or it just overloads.","2":"Return type must be boolean.","3":"Return type must be boolean, not void."},"__rebal":1},{"id":"zf4016","topic":"","text":"Overriding a method means the derived class:","options":["adds a new differently-named method","deletes the base method","renames it","redefines a base method with the same signature"],"correct":3,"explain":"Same name, same parameters - new body.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4017","topic":"","text":"For an override to happen, the signatures must:","options":["match exactly","differ in parameter count","differ in names","differ in return type arbitrarily"],"correct":0,"explain":"Different parameters would be overLOADING instead.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4018","topic":"","text":"class A { void hi() { System.out.print("A"); } } class B extends A { void hi() { System.out.print("B"); } } new B().hi(); prints:","options":["A","B","AB","nothing"],"correct":1,"explain":"The derived version replaces the base version for B objects.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4019","topic":"","text":"An ove