 fleet) total += v.fuelUse();","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4058","topic":"","text":"ArrayList<Object> compared to ArrayList<Vehicle>:","options":["is identical","accepts anything","is faster","only holds Objects made with new Object()"],"correct":1,"explain":"Wider element types trade away useful compile-time interface.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4059","topic":"","text":"The elements of an ArrayList<Vehicle> are:","options":["object copies","primitive handles","references to the vehicle objects","class names"],"correct":2,"explain":"Same reference semantics as every other collection.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4060","topic":"","text":"Removing a Truck from fleet affects the Truck object:","options":["destroys it instantly","converts it","not at all - membership changed","renames it"],"correct":2,"explain":"Lists hold references; objects live by reachability.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4061","topic":"","text":"Counting how many fleet members are Trucks uses:","options":["fleet.count(Truck)","the list size","toString","instanceof inside a loop"],"correct":3,"explain":"if (v instanceof Truck) truckCount++;","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u10/z10_7":[{"id":"zy10_7_0_h3_286_8","topic":"abstract cannot instantiate","_dom":"inherit","difficulty":"hard","text":"Given 'abstract class Shape { }', the line 'Shape s = new Shape();' will:","options":["run fine","throw at runtime","cause a compile error","print null"],"correct":2,"explain":"You cannot use 'new' on an abstract class; you must instantiate a concrete subclass instead. Abstract classes cannot be instantiated.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy10_7_1_px286_inh_6","topic":"Can an abstract class have a constructor","text":"Can an abstract class have a constructor?","options":["Only if it has no abstract methods","Only if it is static","Yes, called by subclass constructors via super()","No, never"],"correct":2,"explain":"Abstract classes can have constructors, invoked by subclasses through super().","distractors":{"0":"Although you cannot instantiate an abstract class directly, its constructor still runs for subclasses.","2":"Although you cannot instantiate an abstract class directly, its constructor still runs for subclasses.","3":"Although you cannot instantiate an abstract class directly, its constructor still runs for subclasses."},"_practice":true,"__rebal":1},{"id":"zy10_7_8_p18","topic":"Must implement","text":"A concrete subclass of an abstract class must:","options":["implement only the methods it intends to call","redeclare every field the parent declared","provide a constructor matching the parent's","implement all abstract methods (or be abstract too)"],"correct":3,"explain":"Concrete subclasses must implement every inherited abstract method.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy10_7_9_p21","topic":"When abstract","text":"Use an abstract class when you need:","options":["a pure contract with no shared code at all","a class that must never be subclassed","shared state and partial implementation","one shared copy of a field across instances"],"correct":2,"explain":"Abstract classes suit shared fields and partial implementations.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy10_7_10_p25","topic":"Abstract subclass","text":"If a subclass does NOT implement an inherited abstract method, it:","options":["throws at runtime","compiles fine","becomes an interface","must itself be declared abstract"],"correct":3,"explain":"An unimplemented abstract method forces the subclass to be abstract.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zy10_7_11_x286_in2","topic":"Abstract class","_dom":"inherit","text":"An abstract class in Java:","options":["Cannot be instantiated directly and may contain abstract methods","Can be instantiated with new","Cannot have any concrete methods","Is the same as an interface"],"correct":0,"explain":"Abstract classes cannot be instantiated and can mix abstract and concrete methods.","__rebal":1},{"id":"fs_z10_7_1","topic":"Concrete method calling an abstract method","text":"What does this print?

