act classes may not","The class is deliberately incomplete: at least one declared method has no implementation, so the object could not answer every call","Abstract classes have no memory layout, so no fields could be stored","Abstract classes have no constructor, so there is nothing for new to call"],"correct":1,"explain":"An abstract class is a partial description, so instances of it could not honour its own declared methods. Its constructor still exists and runs, but only through a concrete subclass calling super(...)."},{"id":"fs_z10_7_6","topic":"Abstract method syntax","text":"Which line is a correct abstract method declaration inside an abstract class?","options":["public double area();","public abstract double area();","public abstract double area() { }","public abstract double area() { return 0; }"],"correct":1,"explain":"An abstract method is a header ending in a semicolon with no body at all. Supplying braces, even empty ones, makes it concrete, and a non-abstract method may not omit its body."},{"id":"zf4062","topic":"","text":"An abstract class is one that:","options":["cannot be instantiated directly","has no methods","is final","is private"],"correct":0,"explain":"new AbstractShape() is a compile error - it exists to be extended.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4063","topic":"","text":"The abstract keyword on a CLASS signals:","options":["the class is fast","a concept for subclasses to complete","no fields allowed","it is a test class"],"correct":1,"explain":"Shape as an idea; Circle and Square as realities.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4064","topic":"","text":"An abstract METHOD has:","options":["an empty body { }","a default body","a signature but no body","two bodies"],"correct":2,"explain":"abstract double area(); - the semicolon replaces the braces.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4065","topic":"","text":"A class containing an abstract method must be:","options":["final","public","static","declared abstract itself"],"correct":3,"explain":"One incomplete method makes the whole type incomplete.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4066","topic":"","text":"Abstract classes MAY contain:","options":["implemented methods and fields too","only abstract methods","nothing but constants","no fields ever"],"correct":0,"explain":"The mix - shared code plus required blanks - is their strength.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4067","topic":"","text":"Why make Shape abstract rather than concrete with a dummy area()?","options":["abstract is faster","a generic shape has no real area","dummy values are illegal","shapes are final"],"correct":1,"explain":"The type system now enforces what a comment could only suggest.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4068","topic":"","text":"Shape s = new Circle(3); with abstract Shape:","options":["fails - Shape is abstract","creates a Shape","legal - abstract references are fine","warns"],"correct":2,"explain":"You cannot NEW an abstract class; you can absolutely reference by it.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4069","topic":"","text":"Forgetting to implement one abstract method in a concrete subclass:","options":["a warning","fine - it defaults","a runtime error","is a compile error"],"correct":3,"explain":"The compiler counts the blanks and demands them all filled.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4070","topic":"","text":"An abstract class WITH a constructor:","options":["is contradictory","cannot compile","runs the constructor alone","normal - subclasses call it via super"],"correct":3,"explain":"The base part of every concrete subclass still needs initializing.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4071","topic":"","text":"Abstract classes vs interfaces (previewed):","options":["abstract classes can carry fields and shared method bodies","they are identical","interfaces hold fields freely in intro Java","abstract classes have no methods"],"correct":0,"explain":"The is-a-with-shared-machinery case suits abstract classes.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4072","topic":"","text":"The abstract method acts as a CONTRACT because:","options":["it has a body","concrete subclasses must provide it","contracts are comments","the JVM signs it"],"correct":1,"explain":"Callers can rely on area() existing for any concrete Shape.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4073","topic":"","text":"Declaring abstract void draw(); in class Widget and no subclasses yet:","options":["fails until a subclass exists","runs draw","compiles - the duty waits for subclasses","is pointless"],"correct":2,"explain":"Abstract types legitimately precede their implementations.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4942","topic":"","text":"Can new ever run directly on an abstract class?","options":["Yes, always","Only with no abstract methods","Only inside subclasses","No - never"],"correct":3,"explain":"Abstract blocks direct instantiation unconditionally; concrete subclasses are the only route.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u10/z10_8":[{"id":"fs_z10_8_1","topic":"Collection declared with an abstract type","text":"What does this print?

