e supplied default when absent","Always 0","An exception","null when absent"],"correct":0,"explain":"It removes the null-unboxing hazard."},{"id":"zyf14_3_3","topic":"Counting idiom","text":"counts.put(w, counts.getOrDefault(w, 0) + 1) does what?","options":["Replaces the count for w with the value 0","Increments the count for w, starting from 0","Adds w only when it is not already present","Removes w when its count would reach zero"],"correct":1,"explain":"The canonical frequency-counting line."},{"id":"zyf14_3_4","topic":"Iteration order","text":"Iterating a HashMap yields keys:","options":["In no guaranteed order","Sorted","Reversed","In insertion order"],"correct":0,"explain":"Use LinkedHashMap or TreeMap when order matters."},{"id":"zyf14_3_5","topic":"Efficient iteration","text":"Iterating entrySet rather than keySet avoids:","options":["A second lookup per key","Duplicates","Nulls","Nothing"],"correct":0,"explain":"Each entry carries both key and value."},{"id":"zyf14_3_6","topic":"Lookup cost","text":"HashMap get is:","options":["O(1) on average","O(log n)","O(n log n)","O(n)"],"correct":0,"explain":"The key is hashed straight to a bucket."},{"id":"zyf14_3_7","topic":"Custom keys","text":"Using your own class as a key requires overriding:","options":["equals and hashCode","compareTo","clone"],"correct":0,"explain":"Otherwise equal keys land in different buckets."},{"id":"zyf14_3_8","topic":"containsKey versus get","text":"containsKey is preferable to get != null when:","options":["The map is very large and get would be slow","The keys are of a primitive wrapper type","The map is being modified while iterating","Values themselves may legitimately be null"],"correct":3,"explain":"A null value and an absent key are different states."},{"id":"fs_z14_3_1","topic":"put replaces and returns the old value","text":"What does this print?

