D"],"correct":2,"explain":"The while loop tests first: a < 10 is false, so its body never runs. The do-while runs its body once before testing, printing D, then stops. This is the entire difference between the two loop forms in four lines."},{"id":"zf4810","topic":"","text":"A do-while loop checks its condition:","options":["before each","AFTER each body execution","never","once at compile"],"correct":1,"explain":"Body first, test second.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4811","topic":"","text":"Therefore a do-while body runs:","options":["zero or more times","exactly once","at least once, always","forever"],"correct":2,"explain":"The defining difference from while.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4812","topic":"","text":"int i = 10; do { System.out.print(i + " "); i++; } while (i < 3); prints:","options":["nothing","10 11 12","3","10"],"correct":3,"explain":"The false condition is only consulted after the guaranteed first pass.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4813","topic":"","text":"The natural do-while use case is:","options":["menus that must display at least once","counting to n","array scans","recursion"],"correct":0,"explain":"Ask, act, repeat-until-quit - the menu loop shape.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4814","topic":"","text":"do { ... } while (choice != 0); keeps looping while:","options":["choice is 0","the user has not chosen 0","always","never"],"correct":1,"explain":"The sentinel exit encoded in the tail test.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4815","topic":"","text":"The syntax detail beginners miss is:","options":["braces","the do","the semicolon after while (condition)","parentheses"],"correct":2,"explain":"do { } while (x); - the trailing semicolon is required.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4816","topic":"","text":"int n = 0; do { n++; } while (n < 5); Final n is:","options":["4","6","0","5"],"correct":3,"explain":"Increments 1..5; at 5 the test fails.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4817","topic":"","text":"Rewriting a do-while as a while requires:","options":["reproducing the guaranteed first pass","nothing","deleting code","recursion"],"correct":0,"explain":"The guaranteed-first-pass must be reproduced somehow.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4818","topic":"","text":"Input validation with do-while reads:","options":["check before asking","prompt and read once","never re-prompts","uses arrays"],"correct":1,"explain":"The must-ask-at-least-once structure fits exactly.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4819","topic":"","text":"A do-while whose body never changes the condition variables:","options":["stops after once","warns","loops forever","skips"],"correct":2,"explain":"Same progress rule as every loop - the tail test spares nobody.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4820","topic":"","text":"while vs do-while choice comes down to:","options":["speed","style points","whether zero runs is legitimate","array size"],"correct":2,"explain":"Might-not-run-at-all = while; must-run-once = do-while.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zy4_1_0_h5_286_1","topic":"do-while","_dom":"control","difficulty":"hard","text":"int i=5; do { System.out.print(i+" "); i++; } while(i&lt;3); The loop body runs how many times?","options":["5","1","2","0"],"correct":1,"explain":"A do-while always executes the body at least once before testing the condition; after printing 5, i becomes 6 and 6<3 is false, so it runs exactly once.","__rebal":1}],"D286/u19/z19_6":[{"id":"zy19_6_1_bp_D286_q8_7","topic":"Validation pattern","text":"To check a password has at least one uppercase letter, the standard pattern is:","options":["Compare the string with its own toUpperCase() result","Loop the chars and set a flag when Character.isUpperCase is true","Check whether charAt(0) is between 'A' and 'Z'","Call String.contains with the uppercase alphabet"],"correct":1,"explain":"The flag-in-a-loop pattern: scan once, flip hasUpper when found, test flags at the end.","__rebal":1},{"id":"zyf19_6_0","topic":"Pattern loops","text":"Printing a triangle of stars requires:","options":["A single loop printing one precomputed string per star","Recursion, since loops cannot vary their bounds per row","The printf width specifier, which repeats characters","Nested loops, with the inner bound depending on the outer counter"],"correct":3,"explain":"That dependency is what makes the shape."},{"id":"zyf19_6_1","topic":"Row output","text":"Moving to the next row uses:","options":["print with a tab character to step down to the next row","println at the end of the inner loop","A recursive call that restarts the outer loop","A second method that reprints the previous rows"],"correct":1,"explain":"Otherwise everything lands on one line."},{"id":"zyf19_6_2","topic":"Rectangle of stars","text":"A 3x4 block of stars needs the inner loop to run:","options":["12 times","1 time","3 times","4 times"],"correct":3,"explain":"Outer over rows, inner over columns."},{"id":"zyf19_6_3","topic":"Right-aligned triangle","text":"Leading spaces before the stars require:","options":["A tab character before the stars on every row","A second inner loop printing spaces first","printf padding, which loops cannot reproduce","Printing the triangle bottom-up instead of top-down"],"correct":1,"explain":"Two inner loops: spaces, then stars."},{"id":"zyf19_6_4","topic":"Counter usage","text":"In an inner bound of j &lt;= i, the number of stars per row:","options":["Decreases","Is random","Stays constant","Increases with the row"],"correct":3,"explain":"Producing the growing triangle."},{"id":"zyf19_6_5","topic":"Exact output","text":"Auto-graded art fails most often because of:","options":["Logic errors in computing how many stars each row needs","Extra or missing spaces and newlines","Compile errors from unbalanced braces in nested loops","The grader timing out on slow console printing"],"correct":1,"explain":"Output is compared character for character."},{"id":"zyf19_6_6","topic":"print versus println","text":"Building a row character by character uses:","options":["println for each character so rows stay separated","Neither - build the whole triangle in one String first, always","print for everything, letting rows wrap automatically","print, with one println after the row"],"correct":3,"explain":"println would break after every character."},{"id":"fs_z19_6_1","topic":"Right triangle trace","text":"What does this print?

