lass, side by side.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2094","topic":"","text":"static void show() { ... } int x = show(); fails because:","options":["x is taken","show is misspelled","ints reject methods","void methods produce no value to assign"],"correct":3,"explain":"You cannot capture what does not exist.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2095","topic":"","text":"A method that reads a variable declared in main:","options":["cannot - only parameters and own locals","can, automatically","can, if the names match","can, on Tuesdays"],"correct":0,"explain":"Pass the value as an argument; method scope does not include main’s locals.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2096","topic":"","text":"Misspelling a call as squre(4):","options":["calls square anyway","is a compile error - cannot find symbol","defines a new method","warns only"],"correct":1,"explain":"Names must match a known method exactly.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2097","topic":"","text":"static int f(int x) { if (x > 0) return 1; } is rejected because:","options":["1 is not an int","if is illegal in methods","the x <= 0 path has no return","x cannot be tested"],"correct":2,"explain":"EVERY path must return - add an else or a final return.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2098","topic":"","text":"Declaring a parameter again in the body, int n; when n is a parameter:","options":["shadows it safely","resets it to 0","renames the parameter","is a compile error - duplicate variable"],"correct":3,"explain":"The parameter already owns that name for the whole body.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2099","topic":"","text":"Using == to compare a returned String with a literal:","options":["may fail even when the text matches","is the recommended style","always works","is a compile error"],"correct":0,"explain":"Returned strings are often fresh objects - use equals.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u6/z6_13":[{"id":"zya6_13_0","topic":"Why validate parameters","text":"Checking parameters at the start of a method:","options":["Slows the program unnecessarily","Catches bad input close to its source rather than deep in the logic","Is only for public methods","Replaces testing"],"correct":1,"explain":"An error reported at the boundary is far easier to diagnose than an exception thrown three calls deeper."},{"id":"zya6_13_1","topic":"Guard clause form","text":"A typical guard is:","options":["if (n < 0) { n = 0; } and continue as normal","if (n < 0) { System.out.println("bad"); return -1; }","try { compute(n); } catch (Exception e) { }","assert n >= 0; placed at the end of the method"],"correct":1,"explain":"Detect, report, and return a defined value — or throw."},{"id":"zya6_13_2","topic":"Divide guard","text":"Before dividing by a parameter d, check:","options":["d > 100","d != 0","d is an int","Nothing"],"correct":1,"explain":"Otherwise integer division throws ArithmeticException."},{"id":"zya6_13_3","topic":"Null guard","text":"Before calling s.length() on a String parameter:","options":["Cast it","Check s != null","Trim it","Nothing"],"correct":1,"explain":"A null reference throws NullPointerException on any method call."},{"id":"zya6_13_4","topic":"Range validation","text":"A method taking a percentage should verify:","options":["It is an int","It falls between 0 and 100","It is positive only","Nothing"],"correct":1,"explain":"Both bounds matter — 150% is as invalid as -10%."},{"id":"zya6_13_5","topic":"Returning an error code","text":"Returning -1 for invalid input works when:","options":["Always","-1 cannot be a legitimate result","The method is void","The method is static"],"correct":1,"explain":"If -1 is a valid answer, the caller cannot distinguish it from an error — throwing an exception is then the better choice."},{"id":"zya6_13_6","topic":"Throwing instead","text":"Throwing IllegalArgumentException is preferable when:","options":["The method needs to report a normal, expected result to its caller","The caller has passed something that should never happen and must not be ignored","The file or network resource was temporarily unavailable","The program has run out of memory and cannot continue"],"correct":1,"explain":"An exception cannot be silently ignored the way a return code can."},{"id":"zya6_13_7","topic":"Where to validate","text":"Parameter checks belong:","options":["At the very start, before any real work","After the main calculation, before returning","In the caller, not in the method itself","Inside a catch block at the end of the method"],"correct":0,"explain":"Failing fast avoids partial work that must then be undone."},{"id":"zya6_13_8","topic":"Array index parameter","text":"A method taking an index should check:","options":["0 < index && index <= a.length (off by one at both ends)","0 <= index && index <= a.length (allows index == length)","0 < index && index < a.length (wrongly rejects index 0)","0 <= index && index < a.length"],"correct":3,"explain":"Both ends, since either violation throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException."},{"id":"zya6_13_9","topic":"Documenting the contract","text":"Valid parameter ranges should be:","options":["Only in a comment inside the method body","In the method's name, using a suffix","Stated in the Javadoc @param description","In the @return description of the Javadoc"],"correct":2,"explain":"The caller cannot honour a contract they cannot see."},{"id":"fs_z6_13_1","topic":"Guards for null and empty","text":"What does this print?

public static double average(int[] a) {
    if (a == null || a.length == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    int sum = 0;
    for (int x : a) {
        sum += x;
    }
    return (double) sum / a.length;
}

System.out.println(average(new int[0]));
