he array sorted so gaps stay at the end","A separate variable holding the number of elements in use","A constant recording the array's total capacity"],"correct":2,"explain":"a.length is the capacity, not the count."},{"id":"zya6_16_2","topic":"Loop bound","text":"Traversing an oversize array uses:","options":["i < a.size()","i < a.length","i < numElements","i <= numElements"],"correct":2,"explain":"Using a.length would process unused slots — zeros or nulls that are not real data."},{"id":"zya6_16_3","topic":"Adding an element","text":"Appending to an oversize array is:","options":["a[numElements] = value; numElements++;","a[numElements++] = value; a.length++;","numElements++; a[numElements] = value;","a[a.length] = value; numElements++;"],"correct":0,"explain":"Write at the first unused slot, then advance the count."},{"id":"zya6_16_4","topic":"Capacity check","text":"Before adding you must check:","options":["Nothing","That the array is sorted","That numElements < a.length","That the value is positive"],"correct":2,"explain":"Otherwise the write throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException."},{"id":"zya6_16_5","topic":"Removing an element","text":"Removing from the middle requires:","options":["Setting the slot to zero and leaving the count","Allocating a new array one element shorter","Shifting later elements left and decrementing the count","Decrementing the count without moving anything"],"correct":2,"explain":"Leaving a hole would break the "elements occupy 0..count-1" invariant."},{"id":"zya6_16_6","topic":"Unused slots","text":"The slots beyond numElements contain:","options":["Copies of the last valid element in the array","Default values that are not meaningful data","Null in every case, whatever the element type","Values that must be read to compute the size"],"correct":1,"explain":"They hold 0 or null, and treating them as data is the classic oversize-array bug."},{"id":"zya6_16_7","topic":"Memory trade-off","text":"An oversize array:","options":["Trades unused memory for cheap appends","Cheap memory use for expensive appends","Fast lookup for slow element removal","Type safety for the ability to resize"],"correct":0,"explain":"The same trade-off ArrayList makes internally."},{"id":"zyf6_16_0","topic":"Capacity meaning","text":"For an oversize array, a.length represents:","options":["The maximum value","The index","The element count","The capacity"],"correct":3,"explain":"The count is tracked separately."},{"id":"zyf6_16_1","topic":"Unused slot values","text":"Slots past the element count hold:","options":["The last element","Nothing","Random data","Default values such as 0 or null"],"correct":3,"explain":"They must not be treated as real data."},{"id":"fs_z6_16_1","topic":"Looping to length vs to size","text":"What does this print?

