calculation methods are trivially testable.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2246","topic":"","text":"static double monthly(double annual) { return annual / 12; } monthly(66000) returns:","options":["5500","550.0","5500.0","66000.0"],"correct":2,"explain":"66000 / 12 = 5500, as a double: 5500.0.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2247","topic":"","text":"Adding a bonus rule later is cleanest as:","options":["edits scattered through main","a second program","a comment","a new applyBonus method in the pipeline"],"correct":3,"explain":"New rule, new named step - the pipeline grows by one call.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2248","topic":"","text":"int pay = weeklyPay(15, 40) + weeklyPay(12, 10); computes:","options":["720","600","120","27"],"correct":0,"explain":"600 from the first job + 120 from the second.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2249","topic":"","text":"The example passes rate and hours INTO computePay rather than using fields because:","options":["fields are illegal","explicit inputs, visible data flow","parameters are faster","main demands it"],"correct":1,"explain":"Same method serves any employee - nothing hidden.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2250","topic":"","text":"static void printPay(String name, int pay) { System.out.println(name + ": $" + pay); } printPay("Ada", 800); prints:","options":["name: $pay","Ada: $800","Ada 800","$800 Ada"],"correct":1,"explain":"The template fills with the arguments.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2251","topic":"","text":"If tax rules change, the method-based design means editing:","options":["every calculation site","all methods","the one tax-related method","the tests only"],"correct":2,"explain":"Localized change is the payoff for the earlier decomposition.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u6/z6_24":[{"id":"zya6_24_0","topic":"Validation method","text":"Extracting domain validation into a method gives:","options":["A shorter main method with the logic inlined","A static field holding the last validation result","A constructor that rejects invalid domains","A reusable, testable isValid(String) returning boolean"],"correct":3,"explain":"The name documents the intent and the boolean return composes into any condition."},{"id":"zya6_24_1","topic":"Return type","text":"A validation method returns:","options":["int","String","void","boolean"],"correct":3,"explain":"Valid or not is a yes/no answer."},{"id":"zya6_24_2","topic":"Helper methods","text":"Checking characters, length and the dot separately:","options":["Runs faster than one combined condition","Lets each rule be tested and read on its own","Is required, since Java limits condition length","Guarantees the rules are checked in order"],"correct":1,"explain":"hasValidChars, hasDot and isRightLength compose into isValid."},{"id":"zya6_24_3","topic":"Early return","text":"Returning false at the first violation:","options":["Requires break","Is a bug","Skips later checks incorrectly","Is correct"],"correct":3,"explain":"The answer cannot change once a rule is broken. One failure decides the result."},{"id":"zya6_24_4","topic":"Empty input","text":"isValid("") should:","options":["Throw","Return null","Return true, since the character loop passes vacuously","Return false via an explicit guard"],"correct":3,"explain":"The loop-only version wrongly reports empty as valid — the guard is what fixes it."},{"id":"zya6_24_5","topic":"null input","text":"isValid(null) without a guard:","options":["Returns true","Will not compile","Returns false","Throws NullPointerException"],"correct":3,"explain":"Check for null before calling any method on the parameter."},{"id":"zya6_24_6","topic":"Validating many domains","text":"Applying isValid to an array of domains uses:","options":["Recursion","A 2D array","Copied code per domain","A loop calling the same method"],"correct":3,"explain":"Which is the entire argument for having extracted the method."},{"id":"zya6_24_7","topic":"Method naming","text":"A boolean method is conventionally named:","