":"","text":"Employee e = new Employee("Ada", 20, 40); e.weeklyPay() returns:","options":["2040","60","0","800"],"correct":3,"explain":"20 x 40 from e’s own fields.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2459","topic":"","text":"Two Employees with different rates calling weeklyPay():","options":["each compute from their own fields","share one result","error","average the rates"],"correct":0,"explain":"Same method body, per-object data - the essence of objects.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2460","topic":"","text":"Compared with static computePay(rate, hours), the class version:","options":["keeps data and calculation together","is always faster","removes the math","cannot be tested"],"correct":0,"explain":"The Employee owns both its numbers and its rules.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2461","topic":"","text":"e.setRate(25); after construction:","options":["changes all employees","changes e’s rate for future pay calculations","recomputes old pay retroactively in printouts already made","throws"],"correct":1,"explain":"Mutators update state; later calls see the new value.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2462","topic":"","text":"A raise method, public void raise(int amount) { rate += amount; }:","options":["belongs in main","cannot exist","puts the raise rule inside Employee","changes hours"],"correct":2,"explain":"Behavior that touches employee state belongs on the employee.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2463","topic":"","text":"ArrayList<Employee> staff with a loop summing weeklyPay() computes:","options":["the largest salary","the staff count","nothing","total payroll"],"correct":3,"explain":"for (Employee e : staff) total += e.weeklyPay();","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2464","topic":"","text":"The constructor Employee(String name, int rate, int hours):","options":["a fully initialized employee at once","runs weekly","must be void","prints the name"],"correct":0,"explain":"Born-valid objects with all fields set.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2465","topic":"","text":"Validation like "rate must be positive" belongs in:","options":["main only","the constructor and setRate","the printout","nowhere"],"correct":1,"explain":"The class guards its own invariants at every door that changes state.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2466","topic":"","text":"public String toString() { return name + " earns " + weeklyPay(); } enables:","options":["nothing","faster pay","println(e) printing meaningful text","private access"],"correct":2,"explain":"println calls toString automatically - override it for readable objects.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf2467","topic":"","text":"Adding overtime later means editing:","options":["every call site","main only","the JVM","weeklyPay inside Employee"],"correct":3,"explain":"Encapsulated logic changes in one place.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u7/z7_22":[{"id":"zya7_22_0","topic":"Domain as an object","text":"Making Domain a class lets it hold:","options":["Only the name, with status kept elsewhere","Only the status, with the name kept elsewhere","One shared status for every domain checked","The name and its registered status together"],"correct":3,"explain":"Two related values that must stay consistent belong in one object."},{"id":"zya7_22_1","topic":"Private registered flag","text":"Declaring registered private means:","options":["It can never be changed once the object exists","It is shared by every Domain in the program","It can only change through methods that enforce the rules","It is visible to every class in the package"],"correct":2,"explain":"register() can refuse an invalid name — impossible with a bare boolean variable."},{"id":"zya7_22_2","topic":"isValid as a method","text":"Moving validation into the class means:","options":["Makes the validation run faster at execution","The validation lives with the data it validates","Removes the need to test the validation","Forces every caller to validate before use"],"correct":1,"explain":"Every user of a Domain gets the same rules automatically."},{"id":"zya7_22_3","topic":"isAvailable logic","text":"isAvailable() should return:","options":["isValid() && !registered","!isValid()","true always","registered"],"correct":0,"explain":"A domain is available when it is well-formed and not already taken."},{"id":"zya7_22_4","topic":"register guard","text":"register() should:","options":["Set it only when the name is valid","Throw always","Do nothing","Always set registered to true"],"correct":0,"explain":"The guard is what makes the invariant hold."},{"id":"zya7_22_5","topic":"Constructor state","text":"The constructor should set registered to:","options":["false","null","Undefined","true"],"correct":0,"explain":"A newly created domain is not yet registered."},{"id":"zya7_22_6","topic":"Validation rules","text":"Domain validation checks:","options":["Only the total length of the name","Allowed characters and the presence of a dot","Only that the name is not the empty string","Whether the name is already registered"],"correct":1,"explain":"Both rules must pass; either failing makes it invalid."},{"id":"zya7_22_7","topic":"Array of domains","text":"An array of Domain objects lets you:","options":["Check availability for each with one loop","Check availability with no loop at all","Store the names and statuses in one string","Sort the domains by registration date"],"correct":0,"explain":"Each object answers for itself."},{"id":"zya7_22_8","topic":"Testing the class","text":"A good Domain test includes:","options":["Only realistic names that a user would type","Only names that are already registered","A large set of randomly generated strings","Valid, empty, missing-dot and illegal-character names"],"correct":3,"explain":"Each rule needs a case that violates exactly it, and the state transition needs its own test."},{"id":"zya7_22_9","topic":"Encapsulation benefit","text":"The guarantee a Domain class provides that a String plus a boolean cannot:","options":["The domain name can never be read by callers","Two