System.out.println(digits(7) + " " + digits(40710));","options":["1 5","1 4","0 5","1 6"],"correct":0,"explain":"A number below 10 has one digit, and every other call strips one digit with integer division and adds 1, so 40710 gives 5."},{"id":"fs_z11_5_2","topic":"A wrapper around a recursive method","text":"What does this program print?

static int max(int[] a) {
    return max(a, 0);
}

static int max(int[] a, int i) {
    if (i == a.length - 1) {
        return a[i];
    }
    int rest = max(a, i + 1);
    return a[i] > rest ? a[i] : rest;
}

int[] a = { 3, 9, 4, 1 };
System.out.println(max(a));","options":["9","3","1","4"],"correct":0,"explain":"The one-argument wrapper supplies the starting index so callers need not know about it. The recursive method compares a[i] with the largest value in the rest of the array."},{"id":"fs_z11_5_3","topic":"Two base cases","text":"What does this program print?

static boolean pal(String s) {
