 splits"],"correct":2,"explain":"pow(b, e) = pow(b*b, e/2) (times b when e is odd) - log-many steps.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4191","topic":"","text":"static int fibM(int n) memoized differs from plain fib by:","options":["a bigger base case","loops","luck","remembering results to avoid repeats"],"correct":3,"explain":"Store results per n; exponential collapses to linear.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4192","topic":"","text":"Recursively summing 1/1 + 1/2 + ... + 1/n uses the step:","options":["1.0 / n + harm(n - 1)","n + harm(n)","harm(n) / n","1 / harm(n)"],"correct":0,"explain":"Each level contributes its term; base harm(0) = 0.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4193","topic":"","text":"A recursive method on ints that recurses on n - 2 needs base cases:","options":["just 0","covering both parities (e.g., 0 AND 1)","just 1","none"],"correct":1,"explain":"Odd inputs skip 0; even inputs skip 1 - catch both.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4194","topic":"","text":"Math recursions mirror:","options":["loops only","geometry","inductive definitions from mathematics","hardware"],"correct":2,"explain":"Base case = induction base; step = induction step.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4195","topic":"","text":"static int count7(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; return (n % 10 == 7 ? 1 : 0) + count7(n / 10); } count7(717) returns:","options":["1","3","717","2"],"correct":3,"explain":"Digits 7, 1, 7 - two sevens.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4196","topic":"","text":"The advantage of gcd’s recursion over trial division is:","options":["the numbers plummet every step","it checks more numbers","it needs no base","none"],"correct":0,"explain":"Modulo plummets toward zero - very few calls even for big inputs.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u11/z11_7":[{"id":"zya11_7_0","topic":"Exploring possibilities","text":"Recursion suits generating all combinations because:","options":["Combinations must be generated in sorted order","Loops cannot be nested more than twice","Each choice branches into a smaller subproblem","The total count is known before generating"],"correct":2,"explain":"Include or exclude each element, then recurse on the rest."},{"id":"zya11_7_1","topic":"Subset count","text":"The number of subsets of n elements is:","options":["n^2","n","2^n","n!"],"correct":2,"explain":"Each element is independently in or out."},{"id":"zya11_7_2","topic":"Backtracking","text":"Backtracking means:","options":["Using a loop","Restarting the program","Undoing a choice after exploring it, to try the alternative","Going backwards through an array"],"correct":2,"explain":"Add, recurse, then remove — that removal is the backtrack step."},{"id":"zya11_7_3","topic":"Base case for subsets","text":"Generating subsets stops when:","options":["n is 1","The set is empty","Every element has been decided","A match is found"],"correct":2,"explain":"At that point the current selection is one complete subset."},{"id":"zya11_7_4","topic":"Cost of exhaustive search","text":"Exploring all possibilities is:","options":["O(log n)","Always fast","Exponential","O(n)"],"correct":2,"explain":"This is why brute force is limited to small n. It is only practical for small inputs."},{"id":"zya11_7_5","topic":"Pruning","text":"Abandoning a branch that cannot lead to a solution:","options":["Is backtracking, and it has no effect on cost","Is pruning, and it can vastly reduce the work","Is memoization, and it stores earlier results","Is a bug, since every branch must be explored"],"correct":1,"explain":"It is what makes backtracking practical for problems like N-Queens."},{"id":"zya11_7_6","topic":"Permutation count","text":"The number of permutations of n distinct items is:","options":["n","2^n","n!","n^2"],"correct":2,"explain":"Which grows even faster than the subset count."},{"id":"zya11_7_7","topic":"Shared state","text":"When building results in a shared list, you must:","options":["Copy the list before each recursive call","Clear the list once the recursion finishes","Pass the list by value so changes are local","Undo your change after the recursive call returns"],"correct":3,"explain":"Otherwise later branches inherit earlier choices — the classic backtracking bug."},{"id":"zyf11_7_0","topic":"Subset growth","text":"The number of subsets of 20 elements is about:","options":["20","8000","400","1,048,576"],"correct":3,"explain":"2^20 — exponential growth limits brute force to small n."},{"id":"zyf11_7_1","topic":"Undo step","text":"After exploring a branch you must undo the choice because:","options":["It is faster","It sorts","Java requires it","Otherwise later branches inherit it"],"correct":3,"explain":"That removal is the backtrack."},{"id":"fs_z11_7_1","topic":"Counting subsets","text":"What does this program print?

