se case of combination generators is:","options":["no choices left - emit the built result","the first choice","an error","a loop"],"correct":0,"explain":"A complete selection is the direct answer.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4203","topic":"","text":"Exhaustive recursion is practical only when:","options":["always","the possibility count stays manageable","inputs are sorted","answers are unique"],"correct":1,"explain":"2^n and n! explode - fine for 10 items, hopeless for 100.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4204","topic":"","text":""Backtracking" refers to:","options":["giving up","looping backwards","undoing a choice after exploring it","deleting the recursion"],"correct":2,"explain":"Choose, recurse, un-choose - the exploration rhythm.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4205","topic":"","text":"Finding whether coins {1, 5, 10} can make 12 exactly:","options":["one division","sorting coins","impossible","try each coin, reducing the target"],"correct":3,"explain":"canMake(t) = any coin c with canMake(t - c); base t == 0 true, t < 0 false.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4206","topic":"","text":"Pruning an exploration means:","options":["skipping provably hopeless branches","random skipping","stopping entirely","sorting results"],"correct":0,"explain":"A negative remaining target need not be explored further.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4207","topic":"","text":"A maze solver trying up/down/left/right recursively must also:","options":["sort the maze","mark visited cells against circling","count walls","use no base case"],"correct":1,"explain":"Progress in graphs requires remembering where you have been.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u11/z11_8":[{"id":"zya11_8_0","topic":"StackOverflowError cause","text":"StackOverflowError happens when:","options":["The program allocates too many objects on the heap","An array index exceeds the array's length","Recursion goes too deep, exhausting stack frames","A method returns a value larger than its type"],"correct":2,"explain":"Each pending call holds a frame."},{"id":"zya11_8_1","topic":"Most common cause","text":"The usual cause is:","options":["A syntax error","A null value","Too much data","A missing or unreachable base case"],"correct":3,"explain":"Infinite recursion hits the limit within a second."},{"id":"zya11_8_2","topic":"Error vs Exception","text":"StackOverflowError is:","options":["A warning","A compile error","A checked exception","An Error"],"correct":3,"explain":"Catching it usually hides a bug rather than fixing one. Normally should not be caught."},{"id":"zya11_8_3","topic":"Typical depth limit","text":"Default stack depth is roughly:","options":["Ten to twenty calls at most","Millions to tens of millions of calls","Limited only by the available heap memory","Thousands to tens of thousands of calls"],"correct":3,"explain":"Which is why recursion depth proportional to n fails on large n."},{"id":"zya11_8_4","topic":"Safe depth","text":"Binary search recursion on a million elements is:","options":["Impossible","O(n) deep","Unsafe","Safe"],"correct":3,"explain":"Logarithmic depth is never the problem; linear depth can be. Depth is only about 20."},{"id":"zya11_8_5","topic":"Fixing deep recursion","text":"A recursion that legitimately goes very deep should be:","options":["Left alone, since the JVM grows the stack","Rewritten iteratively, or given an explicit stack","Wrapped in a try-catch for StackOverflowError","Split across several threads to share the depth"],"correct":1,"explain":"Java does not optimize tail calls, so depth is a real constraint."},{"id":"zya11_8_6","topic":"Detecting the cause","text":"A stack trace for this error shows:","options":["A null pointer","A file name","One line","The same method repeated many times"],"correct":3,"explain":"That repetition points straight at the runaway method."},{"id":"zya11_8_7","topic":"Mutual recursion","text":"Two methods calling each other with no base case:","options":["Is a compile error","Cannot happen","Is legal and safe","Also causes StackOverflowError"],"correct":3,"explain":"The trace alternates between the two names."},{"id":"zyf11_8_0","topic":"Diagnosing the trace","text":"A StackOverflowError trace shows:","options":["A file name","One frame","The same method repeated many times","A null value"],"correct":2,"explain":"That repetition identifies the runaway method."},{"id":"zyf11_8_1","topic":"Depth-safe recursion","text":"Recursion with logarithmic depth is:","options":["Always O(n)","Unsafe","Safe","Impossible"],"correct":2,"explain":"Binary search reaches depth 20 on a million elements. The depth stays small even for huge inputs."},{"id":"fs_z11_8_1","topic":"Running out of stack","text":"What does this program print?

