mited","two frames","thousands of frames (JVM-dependent)"],"correct":3,"explain":"Exact numbers vary; the order of magnitude is what to remember.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4215","topic":"","text":"fib(50) naive does NOT overflow the stack because:","options":["its depth is only about 50","it is iterative","the JVM caches","it does overflow"],"correct":0,"explain":"Depth (frames at once) and total calls are different measures - fib is slow, not deep.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4216","topic":"","text":"An accidental self-call, int getX() { return getX(); } (instead of return x;):","options":["returns x","overflows at the first use","returns 0","warns"],"correct":1,"explain":"A classic typo: the getter recursing into itself forever.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4217","topic":"","text":"StackOverflowError vs OutOfMemoryError:","options":["identical","both about disks","stack frames vs heap objects running out","loop vs branch errors"],"correct":2,"explain":"Two different resources, two different errors.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4218","topic":"","text":"The debugging FIRST STEP on overflow is:","options":["adding memory","deleting the method","rebooting","read the repeating method’s trace"],"correct":3,"explain":"The repeated frame names the runaway; the argument trace shows the miss.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u11/z11_9":[{"id":"zya11_9_0","topic":"Permutation approach","text":"Generating permutations recursively works by:","options":["Sorting the elements and reading them in order","Swapping only the first and last elements","Choosing each element in turn as first, then permuting the rest","Generating every subset and filtering by length"],"correct":2,"explain":"Each choice reduces the problem by one element."},{"id":"zya11_9_1","topic":"Base case","text":"The recursion stops when:","options":["The remaining set is empty","n is 0","Always","One element remains"],"correct":0,"explain":"At that point you output the accumulated arrangement. The built permutation is complete."},{"id":"zya11_9_2","topic":"Number of permutations","text":""abc" has how many permutations?","options":["6","9","8","3"],"correct":0,"explain":"3! = 6."},{"id":"zya11_9_3","topic":"Growth","text":"Permutations of 10 items number:","options":["3,628,800","1,024","20","100"],"correct":0,"explain":"10! — which is why permutation generation is limited to small inputs."},{"id":"zya11_9_4","topic":"Undoing a choice","text":"After recursing on a choice you must:","options":["Return immediately, since the branch is done","Clear the whole result list before continuing","Restore the state so the next choice starts clean","Re-sort the remaining elements each time"],"correct":2,"explain":"The backtrack step, exactly as in 11.7."},{"id":"zya11_9_5","topic":"Tracking used elements","text":"Avoiding reuse of an element requires:","options":["Sorting the elements before each recursive call","A used[] flag array, or removing it from the remaining set","Comparing the element with the previous result","Counting how many elements are left to place"],"correct":1,"explain":"Otherwise you generate arrangements with repeats."},{"id":"zya11_9_6","topic":"Duplicates in input","text":"With repeated characters, naive permutation generation:","options":["Produces duplicate permutations unless you skip repeats","Produces fewer permutations than it should","Fails with a StackOverflowError immediately","Produces the correct set with no extra work"],"correct":0,"explain":"Sorting first and skipping equal siblings is the standard fix."},{"id":"zya11_9_7","topic":"Output location","text":"The permutation should be printed:","options":["Only at the base case","Before recursing","Never","At every call"],"correct":0,"explain":"Only a complete arrangement is a permutation."},{"id":"zyf11_9_1","topic":"Output timing","text":"A permutation should be printed:","options":["At every level of the recursion","Only when the arrangement is complete","Only on the first branch explored","After the recursion has fully unwound"],"correct":1,"explain":"Partial arrangements are not permutations."},{"id":"fs_z11_9_1","topic":"Generating permutations","text":"What does this program print?

static void permute(String prefix, String rest) {
    if (rest.length() == 0) {
        System.out.println(prefix);
        return;
    }
    for (int i = 0; i < rest.length(); i++) {
        char chosen = rest.charAt(i);
        String left = rest.substring(0, i) + rest.substring(i + 1);
        permute(prefix + chosen, left);
    }
}

