andomly","only m2","m2, then m1, then main, then terminates"],"correct":3,"explain":"Frames pop in reverse call order while searching for a catch.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4255","topic":"","text":"The stack trace of that failure lists:","options":["m2 at the top, then m1, then main","main first","only m2","alphabetical order"],"correct":0,"explain":"Top frame = throw site; read downward for the call path.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4256","topic":"","text":"Unchecked exceptions (RuntimeException family):","options":["must be declared","need no throws declaration","cannot be caught","do not exist"],"correct":1,"explain":"NullPointer, IllegalArgument, ArithmeticException - declare-free.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4257","topic":"","text":"Declaring throws on main itself:","options":["is illegal","catches everything","lets the program die with a trace","retries main"],"correct":2,"explain":"Acceptable for tools where crashing-with-info is the design.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4258","topic":"","text":"Catch-and-rethrow, catch (E e) { log(e); throw e; }:","options":["handles it fully","loops","double-throws two exceptions","logs it while still propagating"],"correct":3,"explain":"Observe locally, decide globally.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4259","topic":"","text":"An empty catch block, catch (E e) { }:","options":["swallows the failure silently","is best practice","crashes","retries"],"correct":0,"explain":"Silent failures resurface later with no evidence trail.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4260","topic":"","text":"Methods that validate-and-throw make their CALLERS’ code:","options":["simpler - no scattered checks needed","longer","impossible","recursive"],"correct":0,"explain":"One guard at the source replaces checks at every call site.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4261","topic":"","text":"The exception type in a throws clause should be:","options":["always Exception","as specific as the failure it represents","always Throwable","omitted"],"correct":1,"explain":"Specific declarations document exactly what can go wrong.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u12/z12_5":[{"id":"zya12_5_0","topic":"Creating a custom exception","text":"A user-defined exception is created by:","options":["Implementing the Throwable interface","Annotating a class with @Exception","Extending Exception or RuntimeException","Declaring a class with the throws keyword"],"correct":2,"explain":"Extend Exception for a checked one, RuntimeException for unchecked."},{"id":"zya12_5_1","topic":"Why define one","text":"A custom exception is useful because:","options":["It runs faster than any of the built-in exception types","Its name names the specific failure and callers can catch just it","It cannot be caught by a general catch of Exception","It is unchecked, so callers are free to ignore it"],"correct":1,"explain":"catch (InsufficientFundsException e) is far more precise than catch (Exception e)."},{"id":"zya12_5_2","topic":"Constructor","text":"A custom exception normally provides:","options":["A constructor taking a message that calls super(message)","A static factory method returning the instance","An overridden getMessage() that returns null","A finalizer that logs when it is collected"],"correct":0,"explain":"That message is what getMessage returns."},{"id":"zya12_5_3","topic":"Checked custom exception","text":"Extending Exception makes it:","options":["Unchecked","Checked","An Error","Uncatchable"],"correct":1,"explain":"Extend RuntimeException when you do not want to force handling. Callers must handle or declare it."},{"id":"zya12_5_4","topic":"Throwing it","text":"Raising a custom exception uses:","options":["throws new MyException()","throw new MyException("message")","raise MyException","return new MyException()"],"correct":1,"explain":"throw raises; throws declares."},{"id":"zya12_5_5","topic":"Naming convention","text":"Custom exception class names conventionally:","options":["Start with E","End with Exception","Are all caps","Are lowercase"],"correct":1,"explain":"InvalidAgeException reads clearly at the catch site."},{"id":"zya12_5_6","topic":"Catching a custom exception","text":"A custom exception is caught:","options":["Only by catch (Exception e)","By its own type, or by any supertype","Not at all","Only in main"],"correct":1,"explain":"Catching its parent also catches it, which is why order matters."},{"id":"zya12_5_7","topic":"Adding fields","text":"A custom exception can carry extra data:","options":["No","Yes","Only a String","Only an int"],"correct":1,"explain":"Very useful for reporting exactly which input failed. Extra fields can record the offending value."},{"id":"zya12_5_8","topic":"When to prefer it","text":"A custom exception is preferable to a generic one when:","options":["The failure is common and needs no special handling","The built-in exception types are all deprecated","The failure is domain-specific and callers may catch it alone","The method already declares several other throws"],"correct":2,"explain":"For a plain bad argument, IllegalArgumentException already exists."},{"id":"zya12_5_9","topic":"Exception hierarchy","text":"A custom exception extending RuntimeException is:","options":["Checked","Unchecked","An Error","Not an exception"],"correct":1,"explain":"The compiler will not force callers to handle it. No throws clause is required."},{"id":"fs_z12_5_1","topic":"A custom exception carrying extra data","text":"What does this print?

static class InsufficientFundsException extends Exception {
    private double shortfall;
    InsufficientFundsException(String msg, double shortfall) {
        super(msg);
        this.shortfall = shortfall;
    }
    double getShortfall() { return shortfall; }
}
static void withdraw(double balance, double amount) throws InsufficientFundsException {
    if (amount > balance) {
        throw new InsufficientFundsException("Balance too low", amount - balance);
    }
    System.out.println("Withdrew " + amount);
}

try {
    withdraw(100.0, 250.0);
} catch (InsufficientFundsException e) {
    System.out.println(e.getMessage() + ", short by " + e.getShortfall());
}","options":["Balance too low, short by 0.0","Withdrew 250.0","Balance too low, short by 250.0","Balance too low, short by 150.0"],"correct":3,"explain":"The custom type carries the shortfall alongside the message, so the handler can report 250.0 - 100.0 = 150.0. That extra data is the main reason to define your own exception rather than reuse a generic one."},{"id":"fs_z12_5_2","topic":"Catching a custom exception by type or supertype","text":"InsufficientFundsException extends Exception. What does this print?

