ptions":["unchecked","checked - handling becomes mandatory","uncatchable","abstract"],"correct":1,"explain":"The parent decides checked-ness.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4266","topic":"","text":"Extending RuntimeException instead makes it:","options":["checked","final","unchecked - no declarations forced","invisible"],"correct":2,"explain":"Choose by whether callers should be FORCED to think about it.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4267","topic":"","text":"withdraw(amount) throwing InsufficientFundsException when balance is short:","options":["slows banking","hides the rule","prints only","makes the business rule enforceable"],"correct":3,"explain":"The domain rule gets a name, a type, and mandatory attention.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4268","topic":"","text":"Custom exceptions can carry extra fields, like the shortfall amount:","options":["yes - they are ordinary classes","no - message only","only statics","only strings"],"correct":0,"explain":"getShortfall() on the caught object enables precise recovery.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4269","topic":"","text":"Catching your custom type separately from generic Exception:","options":["is redundant","routes business failures apart from bugs","is forbidden","merges them"],"correct":1,"explain":"Refund the user vs page the developer - different failures, different responses.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4270","topic":"","text":"Naming convention for custom exceptions:","options":["start with Err","end the class name with Exception","all caps","no rule"],"correct":1,"explain":"InvalidDomainException - instantly recognizable in code and traces.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4271","topic":"","text":"Throwing the custom type looks like:","options":["InsufficientFundsException.throw()","new throw ...","throw new InsufficientFundsException(msg);","raise(...)"],"correct":2,"explain":"Same throw statement, your type, your message.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4272","topic":"","text":"Too MANY custom exception types (one per method):","options":["is ideal","is required","crashes","noise - one type per failure CATEGORY"],"correct":3,"explain":"A few well-named domain failures beat dozens of one-off classes.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u13/z13_4":[{"id":"zya13_4_0","topic":"Bounded type parameter","text":"class Box&lt;T extends Number> means T must be:","options":["Any type","Number or a subclass of it","Exactly Number","A primitive"],"correct":1,"explain":"The bound lets you call Number methods on T inside the class."},{"id":"zya13_4_1","topic":"Why bound a type","text":"Bounding a type parameter allows:","options":["Creating new instances of the bounded type","Calling the bounded type's methods on T","Passing primitives as the type argument","Changing the bound while the program runs"],"correct":1,"explain":"Without a bound, T is effectively Object and only Object methods are available."},{"id":"zya13_4_3","topic":"Violating the bound","text":"new Box&lt;String>() where T extends Number is:","options":["Allowed","A compile error","A runtime error","Allowed with a cast"],"correct":1,"explain":"The bound is enforced at compile time. String is not a Number."},{"id":"zya13_4_4","topic":"extends for interfaces","text":"For a generic bound, an interface uses:","options":["implements","extends","with",":"],"correct":1,"explain":"In a type bound, extends covers both classes and interfaces."},{"id":"zya13_4_5","topic":"Multiple bounds","text":"&lt;T extends Number & Comparable&lt;T>> means T must:","options":["Be either one","Satisfy both constraints","Be an interface","Be abstract"],"correct":1,"explain":"A class bound, if present, must come first."},{"id":"zya13_4_7","topic":"Type safety benefit","text":"Generics with bounds provide:","options":["Runtime checking that throws when a type is wrong","Faster code, since the compiler specialises types","Automatic conversion between the bounded types","Compile-time checking, removing casts and ClassCastException"],"correct