erate with for-each","You call size","You print the queue"],"correct":0,"explain":"Iteration has the same problem as printing."},{"id":"zya14_8_3","topic":"Max-heap","text":"To make the largest element come out first:","options":["Call reverse() on the queue after each insertion","Insert the elements in descending order yourself","Set the queue's capacity to a negative value","Pass Collections.reverseOrder() to the constructor"],"correct":3,"explain":"Or supply a custom comparator."},{"id":"zya14_8_4","topic":"Operation cost","text":"add and poll on a PriorityQueue are:","options":["O(log n)","O(n)","O(n log n)","O(1)"],"correct":0,"explain":"peek is O(1) because the head is always at index 0."},{"id":"zya14_8_5","topic":"Custom priority","text":"Ordering tasks by duration uses:","options":["Sorting the list once before the queue is built","A comparator such as (a,b) -> a.minutes","Overriding equals to compare the durations","Inserting the tasks in duration order by hand"],"correct":1,"explain":"The comparator defines what "smallest" means. B.minutes."},{"id":"zya14_8_6","topic":"Typical uses","text":"PriorityQueue underlies:","options":["Job schedulers, Dijkstra's algorithm, and top-k problems","Undo history and the browser's back button","Breadth-first traversal of an unweighted graph","Balanced-bracket checking inside a parser"],"correct":0,"explain":"Anything that repeatedly needs the current best element."},{"id":"zya14_8_7","topic":"Comparable requirement","text":"Adding your own class without a comparator requires:","options":["hashCode","equals","That the class implements Comparable"],"correct":2,"explain":"Otherwise ClassCastException at runtime."},{"id":"zya14_8_8","topic":"peek on empty","text":"pq.peek() on an empty queue returns:","options":["null","An exception","The last element","0"],"correct":0,"explain":"Same convention as Queue."},{"id":"zyf14_8_0","topic":"Poll order","text":"Elements come out of a PriorityQueue:","options":["Randomly","In insert