}","options":["bad number","0","abc","It does not compile"],"correct":0,"explain":"parseInt throws NumberFormatException for input that is not a number, so control jumps to the catch block. This is exactly what happens when a user passes a non-numeric command-line argument to a program expecting an int."},{"id":"zf4843","topic":"","text":"Command-line arguments arrive in:","options":["System.in","a file","the JVM flags","the String[] args parameter of main"],"correct":3,"explain":"java Prog alpha beta - args holds {"alpha", "beta"}.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4844","topic":"","text":"java Sum 5 7 gives args.length =:","options":["2","3","1","0"],"correct":0,"explain":"The program name is not included in Java’s args.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4845","topic":"","text":"args[0] for that command is:","options":["5 the int",""5" - a String",""Sum"",""7""],"correct":1,"explain":"All arguments arrive as text.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4846","topic":"","text":"Using args[0] as a number requires:","options":["nothing","casting (int)args[0]","Integer.parseInt(args[0])","args.toInt()"],"correct":2,"explain":"The string-to-number conversion, with its unit-12 risks.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4847","topic":"","text":"Running with NO arguments and touching args[0]:","options":["gives null","gives ""","prompts","throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException"],"correct":3,"explain":"args exists but is EMPTY - check length first.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4848","topic":"","text":"The standard guard is:","options":["length check, usage message, exit","try/catch everything","sleep","ignore"],"correct":0,"explain":"Usage-message-and-exit is the polite failure.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4849","topic":"","text":"A usage message like "Usage: java Convert <feet>" serves:","options":["the compiler","users who invoked it incorrectly","the JVM","marketing"],"correct":1,"explain":"Programs document their own invocation.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4850","topic":"","text":"Arguments vs Scanner input:","options":["identical","arguments suit scripted/batch runs","arguments are typed live","Scanner is obsolete"],"correct":1,"explain":"Non-interactive automation is the args use case.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4851","topic":"","text":"java Copy in.txt out.txt uses args as:","options":["file contents","numbers","input and output file names","flags only"],"correct":2,"explain":"Filenames as arguments - the pattern 19.5 builds on.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4852","topic":"","text":"Iterating all arguments uses:","options":["args.next()","a while on Scanner","recursion","for (String a : args)"],"correct":3,"explain":"args is an ordinary array - all array skills apply.","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"zf4853","topic":"","text":"Quoted arguments like "New York":","options":["arrive as ONE args element","split into two","fail","lowercase"],"correct":0,"explain":"The shell’s quoting groups words before Java sees them.","difficulty":"medium"}],"D286/u19/z19_7":[{"id":"zyf19_7_0","topic":"Letter grade chain","text":"Assigning letter grades from scores uses:","options":["A loop over all thresholds that returns the last match","A HashSet of grades searched with contains per score","Independent if statements, letting each grade apply","An if-else-if chain ordered from the highest threshold down"],"correct":3,"explain":"Testing the lowest threshold first would catch everything."},{"id":"zyf19_7_1","topic":"Boundary","text":"A score of exactly 90 under "90 and above is an A" needs:","options":["score < 90","score == 90","score > 90","score >= 90"],"correct":3,"explain":"Otherwise 90 is graded a B."},{"id":"zyf19_7_2","topic":"Average type","text":"Averaging int scores into a double requires:","options":["sum % n","sum * n","sum / n","(double) sum / n"],"correct":3,"explain":"Otherwise integer division truncates."},{"id":"zyf19_7_3","topic":"Empty class","text":"Before dividing by the number of students you must check:","options":["All are positive","Nothing","The scores are sorted","The count is not zero"],"correct":3,"explain":"Otherwise ArithmeticException."},{"id":"zyf19_7_4","topic":"Highest score","text":"Tracking the maximum uses:","options":["max += score;","max = sum;","max = score;","if (score > max) max = score;"],"correct":3,"explain":"Initialize max to the first score, not 0."},{"id":"zyf19_7_5","topic":"Counting passes","text":"Counting scores of 60 or more uses:","options":["count = score;","count++;","count += score;","if (score >= 60) count++;"],"correct":3,"explain":"A counter increments once per qualifying score."},{"id":"zyf19_7_6","topic":"Weighted average","text":"A weighted average multiplies each score by its weight and then:","options":["Divides by the number of scores, as with a plain average","Takes the largest product as the representative grade","Sorts the products and reports the middle one","Sums the products, dividing by the total weight"],"correct":3,"explain":"Dividing by the count would ignore the weights."},{"id":"zyf19_7_7","topic":"Formatting","text":"Printing an average to one decimal uses:","options":["printf("%d%n", avg)","Math.round","println(avg)","printf("%.1f%n", avg)"],"correct":3,"explain":"%.1f controls the precision."},{"id":"fs_z19_7_1","topic":"Average without the cast","text":"What does this print?

int[] s = {90, 85, 79};
int sum = 0;
for (int x : s) {
  sum += x;
}
double avg = sum / s.length;
System.out.println(avg);","options":["85.0","84.0","84.66666666666667","84.67"],"correct":1,"explain":"sum / s.length is int / int: 254 / 3 truncates to 84 BEFORE the assignment widens it to 84.0. The fraction is lost silently - the fix is (double) sum / s.length, casting before the division."},{"id":"fs_z19_7_2","topic":"Cast plus printf","text":"What does this print?

int sum = 254;
int count = 3;
System.out.printf("%.2f", (double) sum / count);","options":["84.66","84.0","84.666666","84.67"],"correct":3,"explain":"The cast happens before the division, so 254.0 / 3 = 84.666..., and %.2f rounds to two decimals: 84.67. Casting first is what preserves the fraction; %.2f then controls the display."},{"id":"fs_z19_7_3","topic":"Boundary score","text":"What does this print?

