System.out.println(grade);","options":["A","B","C","It does not compile - grade may be unassigned"],"correct":0,"explain":"score >= 90 is true when score is exactly 90, so the first branch runs: a 90 is an A. Using > instead of >= would wrongly demote the boundary score - and the if/else-if/else chain assigns grade on every path, so it compiles fine."},{"id":"fs_z19_7_4","topic":"Ascending chain bug","text":"What does this print?

